window.__CAPM_DATA=(window.__CAPM_DATA||"")+"\\\"/><\\/div>\",\"stemText\":\"In order to gather end-user feedback, a senior project manager of an Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) project discusses several ideas with the project team and then they draw the following diagram. What tool are they using?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Mind map<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Mind map\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Affinity diagram<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Affinity diagram\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Decision tree ​<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Decision tree\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Data representation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Data representation\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The project manager and their team used the mind mapping technique. In a mind map, several options are discussed and then visually organized.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> This diagram is not an affinity diagram either, as it does not classify a large number of ideas into groups.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The illustrated diagram is not a decision tree because it doesn’t display or help the team choose the best decision among the different alternatives for gathering end-user feedback.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> A Mind map, Affinity diagram, and Decision tree are all data representation methods, which makes option D “Data representation” too generic to be considered the Correct Answer.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The project manager and their team used the mind mapping technique. In a mind map, several options are discussed and then visually organized. Option B: This diagram is not an affinity diagram either, as it does not classify a large number of ideas into groups. Option C: The illustrated diagram is not a decision tree because it doesn’t display or help the team choose the best decision among the different alternatives for gathering end-user feedback. Option D: A Mind map, Affinity diagram, and Decision tree are all data representation methods, which makes option D “Data representation” too generic to be considered the Correct Answer.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":138,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Who should prioritize items in the sprint backlog?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Who should prioritize items in the sprint backlog?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The Scrum Master<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The Scrum Master\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The Product Owner<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The Product Owner\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The cross-functional team members<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The cross-functional team members\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The entire scrum team<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The entire scrum team\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Apart from the development team, nobody should decide the stories’ order in the sprint backlog. Instead, team members should define their own task-level work and then self-organize in any manner they feel best to achieve the sprint goal (Essential Scrum by Rubin, Kenneth S, page 23). The “sprint backlog” is different from the “product backlog”. A sprint backlog is the set of items that the cross-functional team selects from the product backlog to work on during the upcoming sprint. The sprint backlog represents the primary output of sprint planning.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Apart from the development team, nobody should decide the stories’ order in the sprint backlog. Instead, team members should define their own task-level work and then self-organize in any manner they feel best to achieve the sprint goal (Essential Scrum by Rubin, Kenneth S, page 23). The “sprint backlog” is different from the “product backlog”. A sprint backlog is the set of items that the cross-functional team selects from the product backlog to work on during the upcoming sprint. The sprint backlog represents the primary output of sprint planning.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":139,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager is leading a project using an adaptive development approach. How should the project manager plan the project activities?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is leading a project using an adaptive development approach. How should the project manager plan the project activities?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Plan all of the iterations work before the start of the project.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Plan all of the iterations work before the start of the project.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Progressively elaborate the scope based on continuous feedback.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Progressively elaborate the scope based on continuous feedback.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Develop a high-level plan as the project progresses.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Develop a high-level plan as the project progresses.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Execute the project activities described in the Statement Of Work (SOW).<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Execute the project activities described in the Statement Of Work (SOW).\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Planning activities in an adaptive approach entails progressively elaborating the work scope based on the stakeholders’ continuous feedback. The project is split into iterations, and at the end of each iteration, the customer reviews the accomplished work on the product. Then, the customer’s feedback is used to define the detailed scope of the next iteration.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options A &amp; D:<\\/span> Defining all iterations’ work before the start of the project depicts an iterative development approach while implementing activities described in the statement of work depicts a predictive development approach.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Planning activities in an adaptive approach entails progressively elaborating the work scope based on the stakeholders’ continuous feedback. The project is split into iterations, and at the end of each iteration, the customer reviews the accomplished work on the product. Then, the customer’s feedback is used to define the detailed scope of the next iteration. Options A & D: Defining all iterations’ work before the start of the project depicts an iterative development approach while implementing activities described in the statement of work depicts a predictive development approach.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":140,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">When an agile team was discussing the technical choices of their new project during the zero sprint, a senior team member recalled a similar past project that went through some big challenges and ended up being over budget and behind schedule. What should the project manager do next<span><\\/span>?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"When an agile team was discussing the technical choices of their new project during the zero sprint, a senior team member recalled a similar past project that went through some big challenges and ended up being over budget and behind schedule. What should the project manager do next ?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Look for the performance details of the mentioned past project in the Organizational Process Assets (OPAs).<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Look for the performance details of the mentioned past project in the Organizational Process Assets (OPAs).\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Look for the performance details of the mentioned past project in the Enterprise Environmental Factors (EEF).<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Look for the performance details of the mentioned past project in the Enterprise Environmental Factors (EEF).\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Look for the performance details of the mentioned past project in the issue log.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Look for the performance details of the mentioned past project in the issue log.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Since the mentioned past project followed a predictive approach, its performance details are irrelevant.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Since the mentioned past project followed a predictive approach, its performance details are irrelevant.\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Organizational Process Assets (OPAs) include processes, procedures, and the corporate knowledge base. To understand a past project's performance, the project manager should review various documents such as scope, schedule, cost, quality baselines, administrative records, stakeholder register, and issue log. Relying solely on the issue log might not reveal all the challenges faced.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Unlike OPAs, Enterprise Environmental Factors (EEF) do not contain project performance details.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Even if the new project is agile and the previous one was predictive, leveraging documented lessons learned is necessary, as challenges may not be linked to the project approach.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Organizational Process Assets (OPAs) include processes, procedures, and the corporate knowledge base. To understand a past project's performance, the project manager should review various documents such as scope, schedule, cost, quality baselines, administrative records, stakeholder register, and issue log. Relying solely on the issue log might not reveal all the challenges faced. Option B: Unlike OPAs, Enterprise Environmental Factors (EEF) do not contain project performance details. Option D: Even if the new project is agile and the previous one was predictive, leveraging documented lessons learned is necessary, as challenges may not be linked to the project approach.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":141,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager closed all contracts related to their construction project, except one that concerns setting up security cameras. The only thing left for this contract is to go through a quick inspection by an expert in order to check out wireless connection, night vision, cloud storage, etc. Knowing that the security cameras are working fine and that the project needs to be closed as soon as possible, what should the project manager do?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager closed all contracts related to their construction project, except one that concerns setting up security cameras. The only thing left for this contract is to go through a quick inspection by an expert in order to check out wireless connection, night vision, cloud storage, etc. Knowing that the security cameras are working fine and that the project needs to be closed as soon as possible, what should the project manager do?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Close the contract and the project with no inspection<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Close the contract and the project with no inspection\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Close the contract, but keep the project open<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Close the contract, but keep the project open\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Close the project, but keep the contract open<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Close the project, but keep the contract open\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Keep the contract and the project open<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Keep the contract and the project open\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The project manager should keep both the contract and the project open until the seller performs the inspection.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Closing a contract in return requires verifying that the seller has delivered their work as predetermined in the contract.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Closing a project entails conducting several processes and steps including closing out all contracts.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D The project manager should keep both the contract and the project open until the seller performs the inspection. Option B: Closing a contract in return requires verifying that the seller has delivered their work as predetermined in the contract. Option C: Closing a project entails conducting several processes and steps including closing out all contracts.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":142,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager has been assigned to an agile project that is already mid-execution. Which of the following should the project manager check to examine the high-level description of the project scope?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager has been assigned to an agile project that is already mid-execution. Which of the following should the project manager check to examine the high-level description of the project scope?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project charter<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Project charter\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>User stories<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. User stories\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Epics<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Epics\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Work breakdown structure<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Work breakdown structure\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The project manager should refer to the project charter to find the ‘high-level description‘ of the project. The project charter is a formal document that describes the project in its entirety, including <span><\\/span>its objectives, work processes, and stakeholders. This project planning document can be used throughout the whole project lifecycle (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 184).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options B &amp; C:<\\/span> User stories and epics only represent the detailed requirements, not the entire high-level description of the project scope.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The Work Breakdown Structure (WBS) also outlines the detailed requirements of projects that follow a predictive approach.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The project manager should refer to the project charter to find the ‘high-level description‘ of the project. The project charter is a formal document that describes the project in its entirety, including its objectives, work processes, and stakeholders. This project planning document can be used throughout the whole project lifecycle (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 184). Options B & C: User stories and epics only represent the detailed requirements, not the entire high-level description of the project scope. Option D: The Work Breakdown Structure (WBS) also outlines the detailed requirements of projects that follow a predictive approach.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":143,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A predefined budget allocation is a project ___________________.<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A predefined budget allocation is a project ___________________.\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Budget<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Budget\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Assumption<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Assumption\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Risk<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Risk\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Constraint<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Constraint\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Project constraints are limiting factors for your project that can impact delivery, quality, and overall project success. An imposed delivery date or a predefined budget are considered project constraints (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 72).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Project constraints are limiting factors for your project that can impact delivery, quality, and overall project success. An imposed delivery date or a predefined budget are considered project constraints (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 72).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":144,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager has just put the finishing touches on her final project report before meeting with her manager. She spent the last few weeks holding numerous lessons-learned sessions to get feedback from project participants for the final report. For what reasons did the project manager hold lessons learned sessions? (Select three)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager has just put the finishing touches on her final project report before meeting with her manager. She spent the last few weeks holding numerous lessons-learned sessions to get feedback from project participants for the final report. For what reasons did the project manager hold lessons learned sessions? (Select three)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Lessons learned databases are an important element of the organizational process assets.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Lessons learned databases are an important element of the organizational process assets.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Lessons learned meetings focus on identifying individuals accountable for failures and errors.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Lessons learned meetings focus on identifying individuals accountable for failures and errors.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Lessons learned meetings include recommendations for future performance improvements<span><\\/span>.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Lessons learned meetings include recommendations for future performance improvements .\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Phase-end lessons learned workshops represent a good team-building exercise for project members.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Phase-end lessons learned workshops represent a good team-building exercise for project members.\"}],\"key\":[\"A\",\"C\",\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A, C, D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Lessons learned sessions are performed for the purpose of learning from mistakes in order to avoid repeating them in the future. They also serve as an opportunity to identify and establish best practices and build trust with stakeholders and team members.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Lessons learned meetings should not be used to hold others accountable for mistakes made during the project (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 180).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A, C, D Lessons learned sessions are performed for the purpose of learning from mistakes in order to avoid repeating them in the future. They also serve as an opportunity to identify and establish best practices and build trust with stakeholders and team members. Option B: Lessons learned meetings should not be used to hold others accountable for mistakes made during the project (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 180).\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":3},{\"n\":145,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sFM-0\\\">At the end of the project, and during the lessons learned meeting, a project manager presents the following chart, stating that project expenditures over time form a(n) ____________.<\\/p><div class=\\\"class_sFS-0\\\"><img alt=\\\"Source figure\\\" loading=\\\"lazy\\\" src=\\\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\\\"/><\\/div>\",\"stemText\":\"At the end of the project, and during the lessons learned meeting, a project manager presents the following chart, stating that project expenditures over time form a(n) ____________.\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Slanted line<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Slanted line\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>S curve<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. S curve\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Z curve<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Z curve\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Integral curve<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Integral curve\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">S-Curves visualize the evolution of a project cost over a period of time. The name is derived from the S-shape that data usually form, with low costs at the project’s start and end, and increasingly elevated costs mid-project.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B S-Curves visualize the evolution of a project cost over a period of time. The name is derived from the S-shape that data usually form, with low costs at the project’s start and end, and increasingly elevated costs mid-project.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":146,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager facilitates a meeting attended by project stakeholders to discuss a recurring issue with one of the project vendors. As a facilitator, the project manager should: (Select two)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager facilitates a meeting attended by project stakeholders to discuss a recurring issue with one of the project vendors. As a facilitator, the project manager should: (Select two)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Be in full control of the discussion and its outcomes<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Be in full control of the discussion and its outcomes\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Be responsible for taking meeting notes<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Be responsible for taking meeting notes\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Help stakeholders find common ground and solve the issue<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Help stakeholders find common ground and solve the issue\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Provide guidance without interfering<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Provide guidance without interfering\"}],\"key\":[\"C\",\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C, D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Facilitation means assisting others in dealing with a process, reaching an agreement, or finding a solution without personally or directly getting involved in the process, discussion, etc. For the facilitator to maintain an impartial position, they should approach the discussion as an unbiased voice.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C, D Facilitation means assisting others in dealing with a process, reaching an agreement, or finding a solution without personally or directly getting involved in the process, discussion, etc. For the facilitator to maintain an impartial position, they should approach the discussion as an unbiased voice.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":2},{\"n\":147,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A business analyst needs to get early feedback before the full development of the product. What technique should the business analyst use?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A business analyst needs to get early feedback before the full development of the product. What technique should the business analyst use?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Brainstorming<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Brainstorming\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Requirements workshop<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Requirements workshop\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Prototyping<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Prototyping\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Document analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Document analysis\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Prototyping is a technique used to gather early feedback on requirements by presenting a model of the anticipated solution prior to its full development. These prototypes, often referred to as proofs of concept (PoCs), help validate ideas and refine requirements before the final implementation. (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 168)<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Prototyping is a technique used to gather early feedback on requirements by presenting a model of the anticipated solution prior to its full development. These prototypes, often referred to as proofs of concept (PoCs), help validate ideas and refine requirements before the final implementation. (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 168)\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":148,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Which is the most important characteristic of an Agile team?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which is the most important characteristic of an Agile team?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Their ability to create and manage their own work schedul<span><\\/span>e<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Their ability to create and manage their own work schedul e\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Their ability to be flexible and adaptable<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Their ability to be flexible and adaptable\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Their ability to accurately plan the project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Their ability to accurately plan the project\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Their ability to simultaneously work on their tasks<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Their ability to simultaneously work on their tasks\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Flexibility and adaptability are the core principles of Agile<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options A, C, D:<\\/span> All other skills can be developed over time when the Agile team gets to learn from its own experiences.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Flexibility and adaptability are the core principles of Agile . Options A, C, D: All other skills can be developed over time when the Agile team gets to learn from its own experiences.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":149,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">A project manager is overseeing a predictive project within a functional organization. During execution, the project manager faced an issue that wasn’t identified in the planning phase. To address this, additional work needs to be added to the project scope, leading to an increase in project costs. To whom should the project manager escalate the request for additional funds to complete this work?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is overseeing a predictive project within a functional organization. During execution, the project manager faced an issue that wasn’t identified in the planning phase. To address this, additional work needs to be added to the project scope, leading to an increase in project costs. To whom should the project manager escalate the request for additional funds to complete this work?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Program manager<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Program manager\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Product owner<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Product owner\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project sponsor<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Project sponsor\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Functional manager<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Functional manager\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">In a functional organization, the project manager doesn't manage the budget. Thus, they should escalate the need for additional funds to the functional manager. If the functional manager validates their assessment, they will need to escalate their request to the project sponsor to approve allocating additional financial resources. If the project manager was working in a projectized or strong matrix organization, they wouldn't need to raise their request for more funds to the functional manager.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> A program manager, as the name suggests, only handles programs, which is not the case in this scenario.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The product owner’s role is limited to the scrum framework, which is an adaptive approach. If that were the case, the project manager would need to report similar issues to the product owner, who will escalate the matter to the project sponsor.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D In a functional organization, the project manager doesn't manage the budget. Thus, they should escalate the need for additional funds to the functional manager. If the functional manager validates their assessment, they will need to escalate their request to the project sponsor to approve allocating additional financial resources. If the project manager was working in a projectized or strong matrix organization, they wouldn't need to raise their request for more funds to the functional manager. Option A: A program manager, as the name suggests, only handles programs, which is not the case in this scenario. Option B: The product owner’s role is limited to the scrum framework, which is an adaptive approach. If that were the case, the project manager would need to report similar issues to the product owner, who will escalate the matter to the project sponsor.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":150,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">In the project initiation phase, the sponsor requested an approximate estimation of the project cost by the end of the day. What should the project manager do?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In the project initiation phase, the sponsor requested an approximate estimation of the project cost by the end of the day. What should the project manager do?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Create the product backlog items, estimate how many iterations are required to complete the items, and then sum up the cost estimate of each iteration.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Create the product backlog items, estimate how many iterations are required to complete the items, and then sum up the cost estimate of each iteration.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Create the WBS and sum up the cost estimate of each work package.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Create the WBS and sum up the cost estimate of each work package.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Create the cost management plan.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Create the cost management plan.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Provide an estimate based on similar past projects.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Provide an estimate based on similar past projects.\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Given the sponsor's request for a cost estimate on short notice with limited information, the project manager should use analogous estimating, relying on data from similar past projects and expert judgment.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The project manager cannot create product backlog items (a responsibility of the product owner).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Developing the Work Breakdown Structure (WBS) is not feasible due to the time required and the need for team involvement.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Given the sponsor's request for a cost estimate on short notice with limited information, the project manager should use analogous estimating, relying on data from similar past projects and expert judgment. Option A: The project manager cannot create product backlog items (a responsibility of the product owner). Option B: Developing the Work Breakdown Structure (WBS) is not feasible due to the time required and the need for team involvement.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null}]},{\"id\":\"mock-2\",\"title\":\"Full Mock Exam 2\",\"kind\":\"Full Mock Exam\",\"count\":150,\"questions\":[{\"n\":1,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-1\\\">Rearrange the phases of the project team development model Tuckman Ladder in their proper order: <\\/p><div class=\\\"class_s2V-6\\\"><img alt=\\\"Source figure\\\" loading=\\\"lazy\\\" src=\\\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\\\"/><\\/div>\",\"stemText\":\"Rearrange the phases of the project team development model Tuckman Ladder in their proper order:\",\"choices\":[],\"key\":[],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer:<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s43S\\\"><span> <\\/span><img alt=\\\"Source figure\\\" loading=\\\"lazy\\\" src=\\\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\\\"/><\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\">A = Forming: At this initial stage, the project team assembles for the first time. Project team members get to know each other’s responsibilities and skills. This might occur in the kickoff meeting.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\">B = Storming: Team members compete for roles and recognition as their personalities, strengths, and weaknesses emerge. This phase can involve conflict and adjustment as they learn to collaborate.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\">C = Norming: At this point, each project team member knows their role and how to interact with others. Although initial challenges may arise, they are swiftly addressed, allowing the team to progress effectively and initiate their tasks.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\">D = Performing: The project team at this stage becomes operationally efficient. This is the mature project team stage. Project teams develop synergy between each other. Project team members become performant and produce a high-quality product.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\">E = Adjourning: The project team finishes the work and disbands to work on other things.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer: A = Forming: At this initial stage, the project team assembles for the first time. Project team members get to know each other’s responsibilities and skills. This might occur in the kickoff meeting. B = Storming: Team members compete for roles and recognition as their personalities, strengths, and weaknesses emerge. This phase can involve conflict and adjustment as they learn to collaborate. C = Norming: At this point, each project team member knows their role and how to interact with others. Although initial challenges may arise, they are swiftly addressed, allowing the team to progress effectively and initiate their tasks. D = Performing: The project team at this stage becomes operationally efficient. This is the mature project team stage. Project teams develop synergy between each other. Project team members become performant and produce a high-quality product. E = Adjourning: The project team finishes the work and disbands to work on other things.\",\"type\":\"mapping\",\"special\":{\"type\":\"mapping\",\"targets\":[[\"A\",\"A\"],[\"B\",\"B\"],[\"C\",\"C\"],[\"D\",\"D\"],[\"E\",\"E\"]],\"options\":[[\"forming\",\"Forming\"],[\"storming\",\"Storming\"],[\"norming\",\"Norming\"],[\"performing\",\"Performing\"],[\"adjourning\",\"Adjourning\"]],\"correct\":{\"A\":\"forming\",\"B\":\"storming\",\"C\":\"norming\",\"D\":\"performing\",\"E\":\"adjourning\"}},\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":2,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">Creating the Work Breakdown Structure (WBS) is related to which project management domain? (Select two)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Creating the Work Breakdown Structure (WBS) is related to which project management domain? (Select two)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Development Approach and Life Cycle<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Development Approach and Life Cycle\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Scope development<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Scope development\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>Project delivery<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Project delivery\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\"><p><span>Planning<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Planning\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Project work<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Project work\"}],\"key\":[\"C\",\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = C &amp; D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Creating the Work Breakdown Structure (WBS) is related to three domains: Planning, Delivery, and Measurement (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 194).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Scope development is a made-up term. The PMBOK Guide 7th Edition defines eight domains: 1) Stakeholders, 2) Team, 3) Development approach and Life cycle, 4) Planning, 5) Project work, 6) Delivery, 7) Performance, 8) Uncertainty and ambiguity.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C & D Creating the Work Breakdown Structure (WBS) is related to three domains: Planning, Delivery, and Measurement (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 194). Option B: Scope development is a made-up term. The PMBOK Guide 7th Edition defines eight domains: 1) Stakeholders, 2) Team, 3) Development approach and Life cycle, 4) Planning, 5) Project work, 6) Delivery, 7) Performance, 8) Uncertainty and ambiguity.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":2},{\"n\":3,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">Halfway through a sprint, the development team realized that they planned for more work than they could possibly complete. What should the project manager advise the development team to do next?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Halfway through a sprint, the development team realized that they planned for more work than they could possibly complete. What should the project manager advise the development team to do next?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p>Ask the product owner to remove some work items from the sprint backlog <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Ask the product owner to remove some work items from the sprint backlog\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-1\\\"><p><span>Collaborate with the product owner to reprioritize the product backlog items<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Collaborate with the product owner to reprioritize the product backlog items\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-1\\\"><p><span>Continue work and put off discussing this issue to the sprint retrospective<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Continue work and put off discussing this issue to the sprint retrospective\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-1\\\"><p><span>Inform the product owner during the sprint review that some features could not be completed<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Inform the product owner during the sprint review that some features could not be completed\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">First, the development team should collaborate with the product owner in order to remove some work items from the sprint backlog. The sprint backlog is a living artifact that should be updated whenever something new is learned or discovered. Afterward, in the sprint retrospective, the team should discuss how they can improve their estimations.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Reprioritizing the product backlog items won’t help solve this problem. This activity is often undertaken during the refinement sessions with the purpose of making user stories ready for the following iterations.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The agile team should be proactive and should not wait for the sprint review in order to inform the product owner that they couldn’t complete the affected work.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A First, the development team should collaborate with the product owner in order to remove some work items from the sprint backlog. The sprint backlog is a living artifact that should be updated whenever something new is learned or discovered. Afterward, in the sprint retrospective, the team should discuss how they can improve their estimations. Option B: Reprioritizing the product backlog items won’t help solve this problem. This activity is often undertaken during the refinement sessions with the purpose of making user stories ready for the following iterations. Option D: The agile team should be proactive and should not wait for the sprint review in order to inform the product owner that they couldn’t complete the affected work.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":4,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">A project is 50% complete. During its planning phase, the project manager divided the project into 4 consecutive phases. Now that phase 2 is completed, they’re moving on to phase 3. Based on the following table, how much is this project’s Earned Value (EV)?<\\/p><table class=\\\"class_s2Z6\\\"><tbody><tr><td>Phases<\\/td><td>Planned Value (PV)<\\/td><td>Actual Cost (AC)<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td>Phase 1<\\/td><td>$2,000<\\/td><td>$3,000<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td>Phase 2<\\/td><td>$2,000<\\/td><td>$3,000<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td>Phase 3<\\/td><td>$3,000<\\/td><td><\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td>Phase 4<\\/td><td>$3,000<\\/td><td><\\/td><\\/tr><\\/tbody><\\/table>\",\"stemText\":\"A project is 50% complete. During its planning phase, the project manager divided the project into 4 consecutive phases. Now that phase 2 is completed, they’re moving on to phase 3. Based on the following table, how much is this project’s Earned Value (EV)? Phases Planned Value (PV) Actual Cost (AC) Phase 1 $2,000 $3,000 Phase 2 $2,000 $3,000 Phase 3 $3,000 Phase 4 $3,000\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z8\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>$4,000<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. $4,000\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2ZA\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>$5,000<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. $5,000\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2ZA\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>$6,000<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. $6,000\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2ZA\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>$10,000<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. $10,000\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The project is 50% complete, so in order to calculate its EV, the following formula must be applied: EV = (BAC x % complete).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\">The project's BAC is calculated by adding up all of the PVs of the project phases:<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">BAC = $2,000 + $2,000 + $3,000 + $3,000 = $10,000.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Therefore, the project’s EV = ($10,000 x %50) = $5,000.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The project is 50% complete, so in order to calculate its EV, the following formula must be applied: EV = (BAC x % complete). The project's BAC is calculated by adding up all of the PVs of the project phases: BAC = $2,000 + $2,000 + $3,000 + $3,000 = $10,000. Therefore, the project’s EV = ($10,000 x %50) = $5,000.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":5,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">A senior manager has informed the project manager that she will be leading a Fintech (Financial Technology) project. However, after several weeks, the project manager began to feel concerned because each time she asked about the project's start date, the senior manager replied that he was awaiting an official document to initiate work on the project. Which document is the senior manager referring to?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A senior manager has informed the project manager that she will be leading a Fintech (Financial Technology) project. However, after several weeks, the project manager began to feel concerned because each time she asked about the project's start date, the senior manager replied that he was awaiting an official document to initiate work on the project. Which document is the senior manager referring to?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project charter<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Project charter\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project management plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Project management plan\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Scope statement<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Scope statement\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Enterprise resource planning<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Enterprise resource planning\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The project charter is the document that authorizes the project manager to launch the project execution (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 184). It also includes a brief description of the project and its requirements.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Options B &amp; C:<\\/span> the scope statement and the project management plan contain a detailed version of these requirements.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The project charter is the document that authorizes the project manager to launch the project execution (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 184). It also includes a brief description of the project and its requirements. Options B & C: the scope statement and the project management plan contain a detailed version of these requirements.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":6,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Match the following Scrum events with the corresponding activities in the table below:<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sPW-0\\\"><span>Sprint planning<\\/span> - <span>Sprint execution<\\/span> - <span>Sprint retrospective<\\/span> - <span>Sprint review<\\/span><\\/p><table class=\\\"class_s30J\\\"><tbody><tr><td>Activities<\\/td><td>Scrum Event<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td>A. Inspects progress toward the sprint goal<\\/td><td>-----------------------<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td>B. Presents the project’s performance to the stakeholders<\\/td><td>-----------------------<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td>C. Discusses the improvements that can be applied in the upcoming sprints<\\/td><td>-----------------------<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td>D. Provides estimates of the required effort to complete user stories<\\/td><td>-----------------------<\\/td><\\/tr><\\/tbody><\\/table>\",\"stemText\":\"Match the following Scrum events with the corresponding activities in the table below: Sprint planning - Sprint execution - Sprint retrospective - Sprint review Activities Scrum Event A. Inspects progress toward the sprint goal ----------------------- B. Presents the project’s performance to the stakeholders ----------------------- C. Discusses the improvements that can be applied in the upcoming sprints ----------------------- D. Provides estimates of the required effort to complete user stories -----------------------\",\"choices\":[],\"key\":[],\"answerHtml\":\"<table class=\\\"class_s45E\\\"><tbody><tr><td>Activities<\\/td><td>Scrum Event<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td>A. Inspects progress toward the sprint goal<\\/td><td>Sprint execution<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td>B. Presents the project’s performance to the stakeholders<\\/td><td>Sprint review<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td>C. Discusses the improvements that can be applied in the upcoming sprints<\\/td><td>Sprint retrospective<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td>D. Provides estimates of the required effort to complete user stories<\\/td><td>Sprint planning<\\/td><\\/tr><\\/tbody><\\/table><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\">A. Inspects progress towards the sprint goal = Sprint execution<br/>B. Presents the project’s performance to the stakeholders = Sprint review<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">C. Discusses the improvements that can be applied in the upcoming sprints = Sprint retrospective<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9D-0\\\">D. Provides estimates of the required effort to complete user stories = Sprint plannin<span><\\/span>g<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\">Please note that in the real exam, such a question usually comes in the form of “drag &amp; drop”.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Activities Scrum Event A. Inspects progress toward the sprint goal Sprint execution B. Presents the project’s performance to the stakeholders Sprint review C. Discusses the improvements that can be applied in the upcoming sprints Sprint retrospective D. Provides estimates of the required effort to complete user stories Sprint planning A. Inspects progress towards the sprint goal = Sprint execution B. Presents the project’s performance to the stakeholders = Sprint review C. Discusses the improvements that can be applied in the upcoming sprints = Sprint retrospective D. Provides estimates of the required effort to complete user stories = Sprint plannin g Please note that in the real exam, such a question usually comes in the form of “drag & drop”.\",\"type\":\"mapping\",\"special\":{\"type\":\"mapping\",\"targets\":[[\"A\",\"A. Inspects progress toward the sprint goal\"],[\"B\",\"B. Presents the project’s performance to the stakeholders\"],[\"C\",\"C. Discusses the improvements that can be applied in the upcoming sprints\"],[\"D\",\"D. Provides estimates of the required effort to complete user stories\"]],\"options\":[[\"planning\",\"Sprint planning\"],[\"execution\",\"Sprint execution\"],[\"retrospective\",\"Sprint retrospective\"],[\"review\",\"Sprint review\"]],\"correct\":{\"A\":\"execution\",\"B\":\"review\",\"C\":\"retrospective\",\"D\":\"planning\"}},\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":7,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager is in charge of a software development project that follows an Agile approach. During the project execution, they receive a request from the customer to alter a requirement. What should the project manager do<span><\\/span>?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is in charge of a software development project that follows an Agile approach. During the project execution, they receive a request from the customer to alter a requirement. What should the project manager do ?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Block the change request<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Block the change request\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Welcome the change request<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Welcome the change request\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Avoid the change request<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Avoid the change request\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Take the change request to the Change Control Board (CCB)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Take the change request to the Change Control Board (CCB)\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Flexibility is one of the most important aspects of the Agile approach; the scope of work can change in response to new requirements. An Agile, adaptive, or change-driven approach encourages collecting feedback from stakeholders on a regular basis. Unlike the predictive approach, the Agile approach doesn’t involve a Change Control Board (CCB).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Flexibility is one of the most important aspects of the Agile approach; the scope of work can change in response to new requirements. An Agile, adaptive, or change-driven approach encourages collecting feedback from stakeholders on a regular basis. Unlike the predictive approach, the Agile approach doesn’t involve a Change Control Board (CCB).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":8,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">A project manager is managing a project that consists of developing new software for a client. The project manager is collaborating with the client, business analysts, developers, and marketing team, on the project's outcomes and requirements. Who gets to decide the project's scope? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is managing a project that consists of developing new software for a client. The project manager is collaborating with the client, business analysts, developers, and marketing team, on the project's outcomes and requirements. Who gets to decide the project's scope?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1BZ-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>    <\\/span>The business analysts<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The business analysts\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The client<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The client\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project manager<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The project manager\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>All of the above<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. All of the above\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\"><span>Correct Answer = B<\\/span> <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\">The client establishes the project's requirements. After all, the project was issued by the client. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Business analysts and marketers are stakeholders that could influence the project’s scope, but the client has the final say. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The project manager is in charge of meeting requirements rather than their definition. <\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The client establishes the project's requirements. After all, the project was issued by the client. Option A: Business analysts and marketers are stakeholders that could influence the project’s scope, but the client has the final say. Option C: The project manager is in charge of meeting requirements rather than their definition.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":9,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">After getting assigned to manage a distressed project, a project manager reviews the schedule to find out that the previous project manager did not take into consideration procurement delays. Which of the following options represents this scenario? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"After getting assigned to manage a distressed project, a project manager reviews the schedule to find out that the previous project manager did not take into consideration procurement delays. Which of the following options represents this scenario?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1BZ-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>    <\\/span>Critical path activity<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Critical path activity\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Schedule variances<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Schedule variances\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Assumption<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Assumption\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Constraint<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Constraint\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\"><span>Correct Answer = C<\\/span> <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\">The previous project manager made the assumption that the project would not experience any procurement delays. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Options A &amp; B:<\\/span> There isn’t enough information to determine whether the scenario involves a schedule variance or a critical path activity. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The described situation is not a constraint. <\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C The previous project manager made the assumption that the project would not experience any procurement delays. Options A & B: There isn’t enough information to determine whether the scenario involves a schedule variance or a critical path activity. Option D: The described situation is not a constraint.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":10,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager is leading an Agile project where the team works in a continuous flow rather than using iterations. This approach proved to be less prescriptive and disruptive to the team. Which Agile framework is the project manager using?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is leading an Agile project where the team works in a continuous flow rather than using iterations. This approach proved to be less prescriptive and disruptive to the team. Which Agile framework is the project manager using?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Scrum<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Scrum\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Adaptive<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Adaptive\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Incremental<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Incremental\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Kanban<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Kanban\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9D-0\\\">The Kanban method involves pulling work into the system only when the team is capable of handling it. The Kanban method prioritizes productivity and efficiency through its workflow approach. Unlike the Scrum team, a Kanban team does not have predefined roles.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D The Kanban method involves pulling work into the system only when the team is capable of handling it. The Kanban method prioritizes productivity and efficiency through its workflow approach. Unlike the Scrum team, a Kanban team does not have predefined roles.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":11,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Confronting a quality issue, the project manager uses the _______________, a basic quality management tool that applies the 80/20 Rule to identify top-priority defects.<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Confronting a quality issue, the project manager uses the _______________, a basic quality management tool that applies the 80/20 Rule to identify top-priority defects.\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Fishbone Diagram<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Fishbone Diagram\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Pareto Chart<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Pareto Chart\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>PERT Chart<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. PERT Chart\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Flowchart<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Flowchart\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">A Pareto Chart is a vertical bar chart that ranks defects in descending order according to their frequency of occurrence. The Pareto Chart helps the project team focus on the causes that create the highest number of defects. Pareto’s Principle, aka Pareto’s Law, states that a limited number of causes usually produce the majority of defects or problems, which is referred to as the “80/20 principle” or “80/20 rule”.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> PERT is not a chart; it’s an estimation technique that uses a “weighted” average estimate rather than a simple average ( (Optimistic + 4 * Mean + Pessimistic) / 6 ).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B A Pareto Chart is a vertical bar chart that ranks defects in descending order according to their frequency of occurrence. The Pareto Chart helps the project team focus on the causes that create the highest number of defects. Pareto’s Principle, aka Pareto’s Law, states that a limited number of causes usually produce the majority of defects or problems, which is referred to as the “80/20 principle” or “80/20 rule”. Option C: PERT is not a chart; it’s an estimation technique that uses a “weighted” average estimate rather than a simple average ( (Optimistic + 4 * Mean + Pessimistic) / 6 ).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":12,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">At the end of the iteration, a team member informs the project manager that she wasn’t able to finish one of her assigned tasks due to an issue with her laptop. What should the project manager do in order to prevent such a situation from occurring in the future<span><\\/span>?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"At the end of the iteration, a team member informs the project manager that she wasn’t able to finish one of her assigned tasks due to an issue with her laptop. What should the project manager do in order to prevent such a situation from occurring in the future ?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Discuss the issue during the demonstration session<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Discuss the issue during the demonstration session\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Address the issue during the following iteration planning meeting<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Address the issue during the following iteration planning meeting\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Handle the issue during the next daily standup meeting<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Handle the issue during the next daily standup meeting\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Discuss the issue during the retrospective meeting<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Discuss the issue during the retrospective meeting\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = <span><\\/span>D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">An Agile retrospective meeting takes place at the end of each iteration during which the team discusses what happened during the iteration and determines improvement areas for future iterations. The retrospective allows issues to be identified and discussed along with ideas for improvements. Retrospectives are a primary tool for managing project knowledge and developing the team through discussing what went well and what needs to be improved (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 71).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D An Agile retrospective meeting takes place at the end of each iteration during which the team discusses what happened during the iteration and determines improvement areas for future iterations. The retrospective allows issues to be identified and discussed along with ideas for improvements. Retrospectives are a primary tool for managing project knowledge and developing the team through discussing what went well and what needs to be improved (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 71).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":13,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">A project manager is in charge of a project that has an anticipated duration of 12 months and a $120,000 Budget at Completion (BAC). Equal amounts of project work should be completed each month. However, in the fourth month of the project, only 20% of the work was completed. The project manager spent $20,000 to finish the project. How much is the project’s earned value? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is in charge of a project that has an anticipated duration of 12 months and a $120,000 Budget at Completion (BAC). Equal amounts of project work should be completed each month. However, in the fourth month of the project, only 20% of the work was completed. The project manager spent $20,000 to finish the project. How much is the project’s earned value?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1BZ-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>    <\\/span>$40,000<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. $40,000\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>$24,000<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. $24,000\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>$20,000<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. $20,000\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Cannot be determined due to insufficient data<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Cannot be determined due to insufficient data\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2A1-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A3-0\\\">20% of the project’s Earned Value is completed: EV = % finished x BAC = 0.2 x $120,000 = $24,000<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A5-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> $40,000 is the project’s planned value and not its earned value.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A5-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The $20,000 is the actual cost.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A5-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The available information is enough to be able to calculate the project’s EV.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B 20% of the project’s Earned Value is completed: EV = % finished x BAC = 0.2 x $120,000 = $24,000 Option A: $40,000 is the project’s planned value and not its earned value. Option C: The $20,000 is the actual cost. Option D: The available information is enough to be able to calculate the project’s EV.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":14,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">To engage with the project's numerous stakeholders, a business analyst provides the necessary information through e-platforms and blogs. What type of communication is the business analyst using?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"To engage with the project's numerous stakeholders, a business analyst provides the necessary information through e-platforms and blogs. What type of communication is the business analyst using?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3C-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Interactive <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Interactive\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Push <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Push\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Paralingual <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Paralingual\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Pull <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Pull\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Pull communication is when the information is made available to a large audience whenever they need to check it.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Real-time communication involves one or more people exchanging thoughts and ideas.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Push communication, is when the information is sent or “pushed” to the sender without the need for a prompt response.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Paralingual communication is part of non-verbal communication which involves the use of pitch, volume, and tone of voice to express an opinion.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Pull communication is when the information is made available to a large audience whenever they need to check it. Option A: Real-time communication involves one or more people exchanging thoughts and ideas. Option B: Push communication, is when the information is sent or “pushed” to the sender without the need for a prompt response. Option C: Paralingual communication is part of non-verbal communication which involves the use of pitch, volume, and tone of voice to express an opinion.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":15,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">During a prospect meeting, the client insisted that the new website they want to develop must meet some crucial conditions: it must be SEO (Search Engine Optimization) friendly, with a score of 80% or above, and all of its pages must be responsive on all devices and screen sizes. The client is setting the website’s __________________.<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"During a prospect meeting, the client insisted that the new website they want to develop must meet some crucial conditions: it must be SEO (Search Engine Optimization) friendly, with a score of 80% or above, and all of its pages must be responsive on all devices and screen sizes. The client is setting the website’s __________________.\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Definition of Done<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Definition of Done\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Quality Assurance<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Quality Assurance\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Functional Requirements<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Functional Requirements\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Fit for Use<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Fit for Use\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">A Definition of Done is a checklist of required criteria in order to consider a product ready for delivery (Agile Practice Guide, page 151).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Functional requirements describe the product requirements, e.g., website menus, functionalities, services, etc.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Fit for Use is when a product serves its purpose as it is usable in its current state.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A A Definition of Done is a checklist of required criteria in order to consider a product ready for delivery (Agile Practice Guide, page 151). Option C: Functional requirements describe the product requirements, e.g., website menus, functionalities, services, etc. Option D: Fit for Use is when a product serves its purpose as it is usable in its current state.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":16,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager was recently hired for a software development project with a clear set of requirements and deadlines. Midway through the project, the stakeholders requested several new features that were not included in the original scope. These requests are not accompanied by any additional budget or timeline adjustments. What best describes this situation?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager was recently hired for a software development project with a clear set of requirements and deadlines. Midway through the project, the stakeholders requested several new features that were not included in the original scope. These requests are not accompanied by any additional budget or timeline adjustments. What best describes this situation?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Scope creep<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Scope creep\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Earned value analysis<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Earned value analysis\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>Requirements analysis<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Requirements analysis\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\"><p><span>Scope decomposition<\\/span><span><\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Scope decomposition\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9D-0\\\">Scope creep occurs when the scope of a product or project expands uncontrollably without corresponding adjustments to time, cost, and resources.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Scope creep occurs when the scope of a product or project expands uncontrollably without corresponding adjustments to time, cost, and resources.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":17,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Organizations often attempt to deliver projects with limited budgets and incomprehensive requirements. An Agile approach can be adopted to address such complexities. However, without proper communication, this approach won’t achieve its goals. Under this context, how should a project manager communicate?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Organizations often attempt to deliver projects with limited budgets and incomprehensive requirements. An Agile approach can be adopted to address such complexities. However, without proper communication, this approach won’t achieve its goals. Under this context, how should a project manager communicate?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Informally<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Informally\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Formally<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Formally\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Frequently<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Frequently\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Daily<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Daily\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = <span><\\/span>C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Agile frameworks are known for their frequent and straightforward communication where a project manager is continuously checking in with the team to accordingly decide what could be alternatively done to improve the work pace and boost the team’s morale.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Options A &amp; B:<\\/span> Whether you adopt a predictive or an adaptive approach for your project, you have to use formal and informal communication according to the situation.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Daily communication should not be confused with daily standup. Daily standup meetings are held by the agile team members who follow a scrum framework. The project manager or scrum master is not required to attend this meeting, but even if they do, the daily standup meeting should not be their only channel of communication with the team.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Agile frameworks are known for their frequent and straightforward communication where a project manager is continuously checking in with the team to accordingly decide what could be alternatively done to improve the work pace and boost the team’s morale. Options A & B: Whether you adopt a predictive or an adaptive approach for your project, you have to use formal and informal communication according to the situation. Option D: Daily communication should not be confused with daily standup. Daily standup meetings are held by the agile team members who follow a scrum framework. The project manager or scrum master is not required to attend this meeting, but even if they do, the daily standup meeting should not be their only channel of communication with the team.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":18,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">A project manager is leading a project that was supposed to last 6 months. The project is currently in its second year. Which of the following statements best describes the situation? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is leading a project that was supposed to last 6 months. The project is currently in its second year. Which of the following statements best describes the situation?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1BZ-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>    <\\/span>The project scope was not clearly defined<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The project scope was not clearly defined\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project should have been divided into subprojects<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The project should have been divided into subprojects\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project team didn’t protect the scope from changes<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The project team didn’t protect the scope from changes\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project should have been halted after 6 months<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The project should have been halted after 6 months\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\"><span>Correct Answer = A<\\/span> <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\">The project took more time than it should have most likely because the project scope was not clearly defined. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> There is no indication in the described situation that the project should have been broken down into smaller sub-projects. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The project team doesn't usually have the power to approve or disapprove change requests. Changes conducted on the project scope fall under the Change Control Board's (CCB) responsibility. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The fact that the project has exceeded its allocated time means that the sponsor is still supporting the project, therefore the project should not be halted. <\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The project took more time than it should have most likely because the project scope was not clearly defined. Option B: There is no indication in the described situation that the project should have been broken down into smaller sub-projects. Option C: The project team doesn't usually have the power to approve or disapprove change requests. Changes conducted on the project scope fall under the Change Control Board's (CCB) responsibility. Option D: The fact that the project has exceeded its allocated time means that the sponsor is still supporting the project, therefore the project should not be halted.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":19,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">A project manager is assigned to a construction project of a new housing complex that is expected to take fourteen months. During the last planning session, the project team finished decomposing the project deliverables. Which of the following documents was produced during this meeting? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is assigned to a construction project of a new housing complex that is expected to take fourteen months. During the last planning session, the project team finished decomposing the project deliverables. Which of the following documents was produced during this meeting?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1BZ-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>    <\\/span>Work Breakdown Structure (WBS)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Work Breakdown Structure (WBS)\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Organizational Breakdown Structure (OBS)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Organizational Breakdown Structure (OBS)\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Resource breakdown structure<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Resource breakdown structure\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Requirements documentation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Requirements documentation\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\"><span>Correct Answer = A<\\/span> <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\">The process of breaking down project deliverables means the creation of the project Work Breakdown Structure (WBS). <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The Organizational Breakdown Structure (OBS) represents a breakdown of the project's hierarchy. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The resource breakdown structure includes the composition of the project team. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Requirements documentation is a record of product requirements and the relevant information needed to manage those requirements. <\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The process of breaking down project deliverables means the creation of the project Work Breakdown Structure (WBS). Option B: The Organizational Breakdown Structure (OBS) represents a breakdown of the project's hierarchy. Option C: The resource breakdown structure includes the composition of the project team. Option D: Requirements documentation is a record of product requirements and the relevant information needed to manage those requirements.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":20,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager is leading a rebranding project using a predictive approach for the planning phase and an Agile approach for work execution. The project manager receives an email from a key stakeholder requesting an estimation of the project completion date. In order to estimate the completion date, the project manager takes into consideration the team’s average velocity, which is 20 story points, and the fact that the project still has 205 remaining user story points to complete. How many iterations will it take to finish the project work?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is leading a rebranding project using a predictive approach for the planning phase and an Agile approach for work execution. The project manager receives an email from a key stakeholder requesting an estimation of the project completion date. In order to estimate the completion date, the project manager takes into consideration the team’s average velocity, which is 20 story points, and the fact that the project still has 205 remaining user story points to complete. How many iterations will it take to finish the project work?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>10 iterations<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. 10 iterations\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>11 iterations<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. 11 iterations\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>12 iterations<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. 12 iterations\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Cannot be determined<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Cannot be determined\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">If the team maintains an average velocity of 20 story points per iteration, it would take 11 iterations to complete the remaining 205 story points. (205 story points / 20 story points = 10.25 iterations). Since the timebox of an iteration should not be changed, the project team will need 11 iterations to complete the rest of the work.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B If the team maintains an average velocity of 20 story points per iteration, it would take 11 iterations to complete the remaining 205 story points. (205 story points / 20 story points = 10.25 iterations). Since the timebox of an iteration should not be changed, the project team will need 11 iterations to complete the rest of the work.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":21,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A product owner started the day with a sprint planning meeting to discuss and define the goal and backlog of the upcoming sprint. Which of the following options is correct regarding the sprint planning meeting<span><\\/span>?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A product owner started the day with a sprint planning meeting to discuss and define the goal and backlog of the upcoming sprint. Which of the following options is correct regarding the sprint planning meeting ?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A discussion between the product owner, the scrum master, and the cross-functional team<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. A discussion between the product owner, the scrum master, and the cross-functional team\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A discussion between the cross-functional team members only<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. A discussion between the cross-functional team members only\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A discussion between the product owner and the scrum master<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. A discussion between the product owner and the scrum master\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A discussion between the scrum master and the cross-functional team members<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. A discussion between the scrum master and the cross-functional team members\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = <span><\\/span>A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">In the Scrum framework, the sprint planning meeting should include the scrum master, product owner, and the whole scrum team. When needed, other stakeholders can be invited by the team to attend this meeting. During the sprint planning meeting, the product owner identifies the features with the highest priority. The team asks questions to get the necessary understanding to be able to turn high-level user stories into more detailed tasks.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A In the Scrum framework, the sprint planning meeting should include the scrum master, product owner, and the whole scrum team. When needed, other stakeholders can be invited by the team to attend this meeting. During the sprint planning meeting, the product owner identifies the features with the highest priority. The team asks questions to get the necessary understanding to be able to turn high-level user stories into more detailed tasks.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":22,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The project team is required to comply with new environmental regulations that limit the amount of waste that can be produced during the project's execution, where should this situation be added?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The project team is required to comply with new environmental regulations that limit the amount of waste that can be produced during the project's execution, where should this situation be added?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s79\\\"><p><span>Constraint log<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Constraint log\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s79\\\"><p><span>Assumption log<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Assumption log\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s7E\\\"><p><span>Risk register<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Risk register\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s7H\\\"><p><span>Issue log<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Issue log\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">This situation describes a constraint therefore it should be added to the assumption log. The assumption log records all the assumptions and the constraints of the project.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Constraint log is a made-up term.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> A risk register is a centralized repository for documenting and managing risk, which is an output of risk management processes. It includes details such as the assigned risk owner, probability, impact, risk score, and planned responses.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> An issue log is a tool for recording and tracking active issues, assigning each one to a responsible party for resolution and follow-up.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B This situation describes a constraint therefore it should be added to the assumption log. The assumption log records all the assumptions and the constraints of the project. Option A: Constraint log is a made-up term. Option C: A risk register is a centralized repository for documenting and managing risk, which is an output of risk management processes. It includes details such as the assigned risk owner, probability, impact, risk score, and planned responses. Option D: An issue log is a tool for recording and tracking active issues, assigning each one to a responsible party for resolution and follow-up.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":23,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">Which of the following actions depicts smoothing? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following actions depicts smoothing?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1BZ-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>    <\\/span>The project manager postpones taking a decision about the issue to a later time<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The project manager postpones taking a decision about the issue to a later time\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project manager makes a decision with the assistance of the most experienced team member<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The project manager makes a decision with the assistance of the most experienced team member\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project manager takes into consideration the opinions of both parties when making a decision<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The project manager takes into consideration the opinions of both parties when making a decision\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project manager downplays the issue between conflicting parties<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The project manager downplays the issue between conflicting parties\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\"><span>Correct Answer = D<\\/span> <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\">Smoothing means smoothing away the issue by minimizing its perceived scale. Postponing decision-making depicts withdrawal. Taking a decision based on a 3rd party's input (the experienced team member) represents forcing. Taking into account both parties' opinions is known as compromise. <\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Smoothing means smoothing away the issue by minimizing its perceived scale. Postponing decision-making depicts withdrawal. Taking a decision based on a 3rd party's input (the experienced team member) represents forcing. Taking into account both parties' opinions is known as compromise.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":24,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">A project manager is leading a new predictive project. To evaluate all change requests, a Change Control Board (CCB) has been established, in which the project sponsor is a member. One month into the project, the CCB received three change requests; the first from the sponsor, the second from a low-power stakeholder, and the third one was issued by a senior team member. Which of these individuals is not allowed to submit a change request?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is leading a new predictive project. To evaluate all change requests, a Change Control Board (CCB) has been established, in which the project sponsor is a member. One month into the project, the CCB received three change requests; the first from the sponsor, the second from a low-power stakeholder, and the third one was issued by a senior team member. Which of these individuals is not allowed to submit a change request?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The sponsor since they are a member of the CCB<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The sponsor since they are a member of the CCB\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The stakeholder since they have low power<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The stakeholder since they have low power\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The senior team member since they are part of the project team<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The senior team member since they are part of the project team\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>All of the above are allowed to submit a change request<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. All of the above are allowed to submit a change request\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Change requests may be submitted by any stakeholder involved with the project. The project sponsor(s), stakeholders, and the project team are all considered project stakeholders, therefore, they can all make change requests. CCB membership, power level, or involvement in project execution should not be restrictions for someone to request changes.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Change requests may be submitted by any stakeholder involved with the project. The project sponsor(s), stakeholders, and the project team are all considered project stakeholders, therefore, they can all make change requests. CCB membership, power level, or involvement in project execution should not be restrictions for someone to request changes.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":25,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">After completing all requirements, the project manager sits with the product manager to go over each item of the deliverable acceptance criteria. The product manager found that among thirty deliverables, two did not meet requirements, so they asked the project manager to make the necessary changes before signing off the final delivery document. Which process are they both currently performing?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"After completing all requirements, the project manager sits with the product manager to go over each item of the deliverable acceptance criteria. The product manager found that among thirty deliverables, two did not meet requirements, so they asked the project manager to make the necessary changes before signing off the final delivery document. Which process are they both currently performing?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Control quality<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Control quality\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Control scope<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Control scope\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Validate scope<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Validate scope\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Close projec<span><\\/span>t<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Close projec t\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">During the “Validate scope” process, deliverables are compared against the acceptance criteria and requirements in order to formally sign off the completed deliverables. “Validate Scope” consists of formalizing the approval and acceptance of the completed project deliverables. One of the outputs of the “Validate Scope” process is the accepted deliverables that were formally signed off and approved by the authorized stakeholder.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Options A &amp; B:<\\/span> “Control quality” and “Control scope” should be carried out before the “Validate scope” process. The veriﬁed deliverables obtained upon conducting the “Control Quality” process are the input of the “Validate Scope” process.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C During the “Validate scope” process, deliverables are compared against the acceptance criteria and requirements in order to formally sign off the completed deliverables. “Validate Scope” consists of formalizing the approval and acceptance of the completed project deliverables. One of the outputs of the “Validate Scope” process is the accepted deliverables that were formally signed off and approved by the authorized stakeholder. Options A & B: “Control quality” and “Control scope” should be carried out before the “Validate scope” process. The veriﬁed deliverables obtained upon conducting the “Control Quality” process are the input of the “Validate Scope” process.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":26,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">What are the roles of a project manager? (Select three)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What are the roles of a project manager? (Select three)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Demonstrate leadership<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Demonstrate leadership\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Has a short focus<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Has a short focus\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Has a long-term vision<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Has a long-term vision\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Build trust among team members<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Build trust among team members\"}],\"key\":[\"A\",\"C\",\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A, C, <span><\\/span>D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">A project manager should guide and motivate the team, making strategic decisions and resolving conflicts to keep the project on track. Project managers think beyond the immediate tasks and challenges, planning for the future and aligning project goals with broader organizational objectives. Building and maintaining trust is crucial for effective team collaboration and morale, helping to ensure that team members are engaged and committed to the project’s success.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A, C, D A project manager should guide and motivate the team, making strategic decisions and resolving conflicts to keep the project on track. Project managers think beyond the immediate tasks and challenges, planning for the future and aligning project goals with broader organizational objectives. Building and maintaining trust is crucial for effective team collaboration and morale, helping to ensure that team members are engaged and committed to the project’s success.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":3},{\"n\":27,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">One month into project execution, the project manager notices that the sponsor is always late for their weekly meetings. However, the project manager chooses not to address the sponsor’s behavior. Instead, they document the frequent tardiness in the meetings’ notes. Which conflict resolution technique is the project manager using?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"One month into project execution, the project manager notices that the sponsor is always late for their weekly meetings. However, the project manager chooses not to address the sponsor’s behavior. Instead, they document the frequent tardiness in the meetings’ notes. Which conflict resolution technique is the project manager using?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Problem-solving<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Problem-solving\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Smoothing<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Smoothing\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Information recording<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Information recording\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Withdrawal<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Withdrawal\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The unwillingness to deal with a conflict is referred to as withdrawing. This conflict resolution technique is acceptable when some time to cool off is needed in order to achieve a better understanding of the situation, or when the other party is unassailable or uncooperative (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 169).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The situation does not imply problem-solving since the project manager didn’t point out the issue to the sponsor in order to find a solution.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The project manager didn’t smooth the conflict either since there was no discussion with the sponsor to diminish their differences.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Information recording, taking notes, or documenting the situation is not a conflict resolution technique.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D The unwillingness to deal with a conflict is referred to as withdrawing. This conflict resolution technique is acceptable when some time to cool off is needed in order to achieve a better understanding of the situation, or when the other party is unassailable or uncooperative (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 169). Option A: The situation does not imply problem-solving since the project manager didn’t point out the issue to the sponsor in order to find a solution. Option B: The project manager didn’t smooth the conflict either since there was no discussion with the sponsor to diminish their differences. Option C: Information recording, taking notes, or documenting the situation is not a conflict resolution technique.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":28,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">A(n) _____________________ helps stakeholders check out the status of material shortages, technical difficulties, scheduling conflicts, etc., and how they’re being monitored and treated. <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A(n) _____________________ helps stakeholders check out the status of material shortages, technical difficulties, scheduling conflicts, etc., and how they’re being monitored and treated.\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3C-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Feedback log <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Feedback log\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Issue Log <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Issue Log\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Sprint backlog <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Sprint backlog\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Change log <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Change log\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\"><span>Correct Answer = B<\\/span> <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\">Material shortage, technical difficulties, scheduling conflicts, etc. are problems that should be recorded in the issue log. An issue log allows stakeholders to record and monitor active issues and their status; who’s assigned to follow up and resolve a particular issue, for instance. <\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Material shortage, technical difficulties, scheduling conflicts, etc. are problems that should be recorded in the issue log. An issue log allows stakeholders to record and monitor active issues and their status; who’s assigned to follow up and resolve a particular issue, for instance.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":29,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">A project manager collaborates with the project team to create the Work Breakdown Structure (WBS) for their project. What purpose does this document serve? (Select two) <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager collaborates with the project team to create the Work Breakdown Structure (WBS) for their project. What purpose does this document serve? (Select two)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1BZ-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>    <\\/span>Help the project team define the project scope<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Help the project team define the project scope\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Help the project team visualize the project work<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Help the project team visualize the project work\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Help the project team organize the project scope<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Help the project team organize the project scope\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Help the project team identify the project requirements<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Help the project team identify the project requirements\"}],\"key\":[\"B\",\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\"><span>Correct Answer = B, C<\\/span> <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\">The purpose of creating the Work Breakdown Structure (WBS) is to both organize and visualize the project scope. This document organizes work into work packages and assigns each package a code of accounts. Besides, as a visual tool, the WBS helps the team check the overall work plan, see how the project should progress, and appropriately manage the project workflow. The WBS is developed after identifying the project requirements and defining its scope. <\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B, C The purpose of creating the Work Breakdown Structure (WBS) is to both organize and visualize the project scope. This document organizes work into work packages and assigns each package a code of accounts. Besides, as a visual tool, the WBS helps the team check the overall work plan, see how the project should progress, and appropriately manage the project workflow. The WBS is developed after identifying the project requirements and defining its scope.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":2},{\"n\":30,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager uses the scrum framework to manage a graphic design project. Which of the following events will not be used by the project team?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager uses the scrum framework to manage a graphic design project. Which of the following events will not be used by the project team?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Sprint planning<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Sprint planning\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Weekly scrum<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Weekly scrum\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Sprint review<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Sprint review\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Sprint retrospective<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Sprint retrospective\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Scrum teams use four main events: sprint planning, daily scrum, sprint review, and sprint retrospective.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Scrum teams use four main events: sprint planning, daily scrum, sprint review, and sprint retrospective.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":31,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A business analyst wants to ensure that the requirements align with and fulfill the business goals and objectives. Which process should the business analyst use?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A business analyst wants to ensure that the requirements align with and fulfill the business goals and objectives. Which process should the business analyst use?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Verify requirements<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Verify requirements\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Validate requirements<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Validate requirements\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>Define and elaborate requirements<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Define and elaborate requirements\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\"><p><span>Define acceptance criteria<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Define acceptance criteria\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Validate requirements is about ensuring that the requirements fulfill the business goals and objectives, confirming that they are the right requirements to achieve the intended outcomes (PMI Guide to business analysis, page 175)<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Verify requirements is the process of ensuring that the requirements are of sufficient quality, such as clarity, consistency, and completeness.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Define and elaborate requirements is the process of refining, documenting, and detailing the requirements and other product information to ensure they are understandable and usable by various audiences.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Define acceptance criteria is the process of obtaining agreement on what would constitute proof that one or more aspects of a solution have been developed successfully.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Validate requirements is about ensuring that the requirements fulfill the business goals and objectives, confirming that they are the right requirements to achieve the intended outcomes (PMI Guide to business analysis, page 175) . Option A: Verify requirements is the process of ensuring that the requirements are of sufficient quality, such as clarity, consistency, and completeness. Option C: Define and elaborate requirements is the process of refining, documenting, and detailing the requirements and other product information to ensure they are understandable and usable by various audiences. Option D: Define acceptance criteria is the process of obtaining agreement on what would constitute proof that one or more aspects of a solution have been developed successfully.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":32,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">In which project development approach is a high-level traceability and monitoring approach established early during the planning phase?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In which project development approach is a high-level traceability and monitoring approach established early during the planning phase?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Predictive<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Predictive\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Adaptive<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Adaptive\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>Incremental<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Incremental\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\"><p><span>Iterative<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Iterative\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">A high-level approach for traceability and monitoring is established early in the planning phase in the case of a predictive approach. This approach is refined and adjusted throughout the course of the project. Typically, substantial elements of product information and deliverables are tracked (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 257).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> In an adaptive approach, traceability and monitoring may be outlined at a high level during iteration 0. However, tracing and managing changes to product information are often not considered.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A A high-level approach for traceability and monitoring is established early in the planning phase in the case of a predictive approach. This approach is refined and adjusted throughout the course of the project. Typically, substantial elements of product information and deliverables are tracked (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 257). Option B: In an adaptive approach, traceability and monitoring may be outlined at a high level during iteration 0. However, tracing and managing changes to product information are often not considered.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":33,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">When performing earned value measurements, a project manager finds out that the Cost Performance Index (CPI) of their project is 0.91. What does this indicate? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"When performing earned value measurements, a project manager finds out that the Cost Performance Index (CPI) of their project is 0.91. What does this indicate?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3C-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project is behind schedule <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The project is behind schedule\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project is ahead of schedule<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The project is ahead of schedule\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>91% of project work is finished<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. 91% of project work is finished\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project is over budget<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The project is over budget\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2A1-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A3-0\\\">Since it’s less than one, a 0.91 CPI indicates that the project is over budget; meaning that the project spent more money than expected. There is no evidence that the project is behind or ahead of schedule.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Since it’s less than one, a 0.91 CPI indicates that the project is over budget; meaning that the project spent more money than expected. There is no evidence that the project is behind or ahead of schedule.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":34,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Working in a risk-averse organization, the project manager suggested using the agile approach for a new project that has a high level of uncertainty. How should risk management be conducted in this case? (Select two)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Working in a risk-averse organization, the project manager suggested using the agile approach for a new project that has a high level of uncertainty. How should risk management be conducted in this case? (Select two)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project manager is responsible for managing the risks.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The project manager is responsible for managing the risks.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Both the project manager and the project team conduct risk analysis, determine risk responses, and update the Risk Register<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Both the project manager and the project team conduct risk analysis, determine risk responses, and update the Risk Register\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project team analyzes and addresses risks in all planning meetings<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The project team analyzes and addresses risks in all planning meetings\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Risks are monitored by the product owner during the backlog refinement meeting.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Risks are monitored by the product owner during the backlog refinement meeting.\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">When managing an Agile project, risk identification occurs in all types of planning meetings, such as daily stand-ups, release meetings, iteration reviews, and retrospectives.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> In Agile projects, the project team owns Risk management, while the project manager is only responsible for facilitating the process.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The project team analyzes and addresses risks during planning meetings, then updates the product backlog accordingly. Risk Register is used in the predictive approach.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Even though backlog refinement could be used to address risks, it’s not the only meeting where risks should be monitored.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C When managing an Agile project, risk identification occurs in all types of planning meetings, such as daily stand-ups, release meetings, iteration reviews, and retrospectives. Option A: In Agile projects, the project team owns Risk management, while the project manager is only responsible for facilitating the process. Option B: The project team analyzes and addresses risks during planning meetings, then updates the product backlog accordingly. Risk Register is used in the predictive approach. Option D: Even though backlog refinement could be used to address risks, it’s not the only meeting where risks should be monitored.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":true,\"sourceIssue\":\"Source inconsistency: the prompt says “Select 2”, but the EPUB answer key lists C. This item requires manual review and is not auto-scored until you mark it correct or incorrect.\",\"selectCount\":2},{\"n\":35,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Which factor should be considered during Sprint Planning?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which factor should be considered during Sprint Planning?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Number of stories in the product backlog<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Number of stories in the product backlog\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Number of stories completed in the last sprint<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Number of stories completed in the last sprint\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Team velocity<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Team velocity\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Team size<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Team size\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Team velocity, i.e., the sum of story points’ sizes of the completed features in the current iteration, allows the team to plan its next iteration more accurately by taking into consideration their historical performance (Agile Practice Guide, page 64).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Team velocity, i.e., the sum of story points’ sizes of the completed features in the current iteration, allows the team to plan its next iteration more accurately by taking into consideration their historical performance (Agile Practice Guide, page 64).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":36,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Which technique is used to display a sequence or navigation through a series of images or illustrations?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which technique is used to display a sequence or navigation through a series of images or illustrations?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\" id=\\\"page_131\\\"><p><span>Brainstorming<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Brainstorming\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Wireframes<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Wireframes\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>Collaborative games<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Collaborative games\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\"><p><span>Storyboarding<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Storyboarding\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Storyboarding is a prototyping technique that involves creating a visual representation of a sequence of events or steps. (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 168)<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Brainstorming is a technique used to generate a wide range of ideas or solutions. It focuses on idea generation rather than visualizing a sequence or navigation.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Wireframes are low-fidelity visual representations of a web page or application interface, used to outline the layout and structure. While wireframes are also a prototyping technique and can show the general flow and structure of an interface, they don't typically detail a sequence of images or illustrations.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Collaborative games are interactive activities designed to encourage teamwork and creativity.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Storyboarding is a prototyping technique that involves creating a visual representation of a sequence of events or steps. (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 168) Option A: Brainstorming is a technique used to generate a wide range of ideas or solutions. It focuses on idea generation rather than visualizing a sequence or navigation. Option B: Wireframes are low-fidelity visual representations of a web page or application interface, used to outline the layout and structure. While wireframes are also a prototyping technique and can show the general flow and structure of an interface, they don't typically detail a sequence of images or illustrations. Option C: Collaborative games are interactive activities designed to encourage teamwork and creativity.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":37,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Now that the project is nearly finished, a key stakeholder asked the project manager whether they were nervous about the project deliverables approval process, to which the latter replied that they were confident that the customer would be satisfied with the result. What can ensure the satisfaction of the project’s customer?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Now that the project is nearly finished, a key stakeholder asked the project manager whether they were nervous about the project deliverables approval process, to which the latter replied that they were confident that the customer would be satisfied with the result. What can ensure the satisfaction of the project’s customer?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project’s low running costs<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The project’s low running costs\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>How good the project manager’s relationship is with the project’s end-users and stakeholders<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. How good the project manager’s relationship is with the project’s end-users and stakeholders\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The efficiency of the warranty service<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The efficiency of the warranty service\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Delivering value and conforming to project requirements<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Delivering value and conforming to project requirements\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">It’s not enough to complete a project on time and under budget. You need to deliver value by creating a suitable product for your stakeholders’ needs. Customer satisfaction is about making sure that the people who are paying for the end product are happy with what they ultimately get. Conformance to requirements and usability of deliverables is the basis of customer satisfaction as they allow you to measure how well your product meets expectations.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D It’s not enough to complete a project on time and under budget. You need to deliver value by creating a suitable product for your stakeholders’ needs. Customer satisfaction is about making sure that the people who are paying for the end product are happy with what they ultimately get. Conformance to requirements and usability of deliverables is the basis of customer satisfaction as they allow you to measure how well your product meets expectations.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":38,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">A Project manager ensures that the project team documents all assumptions. The team records assumptions on an ongoing basis and then validates these assumptions. Which of the following helps the team validate a project assumption? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A Project manager ensures that the project team documents all assumptions. The team records assumptions on an ongoing basis and then validates these assumptions. Which of the following helps the team validate a project assumption?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1BZ-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>    <\\/span>Organizational policies<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Organizational policies\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Historical data<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Historical data\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Constraints<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Constraints\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Team members recollection<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Team members recollection\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\"><span>Correct Answer = B<\\/span> <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\">Historical data is the most useful when it comes to validating project assumptions. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Organizational rules help establish the project parameters rather than validate assumptions. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Constraints can’t help the project team confirm an assumption. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Team members' recollections or memories are not reliable since they’re not recorded. The team can use past experiences, documentation, proof, feedback, and any previously completed projects or project work as historical data to verify if a particular assumption is correct or realistic. <\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Historical data is the most useful when it comes to validating project assumptions. Option A: Organizational rules help establish the project parameters rather than validate assumptions. Option C: Constraints can’t help the project team confirm an assumption. Option D: Team members' recollections or memories are not reliable since they’re not recorded. The team can use past experiences, documentation, proof, feedback, and any previously completed projects or project work as historical data to verify if a particular assumption is correct or realistic.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":39,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">The project cost is lower than the project manager had anticipated. The project manager must spend all of the first phase's allocated budget, otherwise, the budget of the second phase will be reduced. To use up the assigned budget for the first phase, the project manager decides to purchase better instruments to offer the client higher-quality deliverables. This scenario depicts: <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The project cost is lower than the project manager had anticipated. The project manager must spend all of the first phase's allocated budget, otherwise, the budget of the second phase will be reduced. To use up the assigned budget for the first phase, the project manager decides to purchase better instruments to offer the client higher-quality deliverables. This scenario depicts:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1BZ-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>    <\\/span>Integrated change control<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Integrated change control\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Effective cost management<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Effective cost management\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Gold plating<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Gold plating\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Budget compliance<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Budget compliance\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\"><span>Correct Answer = C<\\/span> <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\">Attempting to produce deliverables of a higher quality than required to exhaust the allocated budget and satisfy the project client is known as gold plating. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The Integrated change control process consists of reviewing, approving or rejecting, and managing change requests, which is not the case here. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The described scenario depicts poor project and cost management. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Budget compliance is an irrelevant concept used in the information security domain.<span><\\/span> <\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Attempting to produce deliverables of a higher quality than required to exhaust the allocated budget and satisfy the project client is known as gold plating. Option A: The Integrated change control process consists of reviewing, approving or rejecting, and managing change requests, which is not the case here. Option B: The described scenario depicts poor project and cost management. Option D: Budget compliance is an irrelevant concept used in the information security domain.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":40,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager is using the Agile approach to manage a software development project. During a meeting with the team, the project manager presents the _____________ to showcase how much work still needs to be done during the current iteration.<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is using the Agile approach to manage a software development project. During a meeting with the team, the project manager presents the _____________ to showcase how much work still needs to be done during the current iteration.\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Schedule<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Schedule\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Burnup chart<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Burnup chart\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Milestone chart<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Milestone chart\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Burndown char<span><\\/span>t<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Burndown char t\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Unlike the burnup chart which shows the completed work, a burndown chart is a graphical depiction of the work that still needs to be completed (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, pages 108).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Unlike the burnup chart which shows the completed work, a burndown chart is a graphical depiction of the work that still needs to be completed (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, pages 108).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":41,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Depending on who is using them, bids, tenders, and quotes can take on different meanings. But, initially, all of these terms can be used interchangeably with:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Depending on who is using them, bids, tenders, and quotes can take on different meanings. But, initially, all of these terms can be used interchangeably with:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Proposals<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Proposals\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Make-or-buy decisions<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Make-or-buy decisions\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Buyer responses<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Buyer responses\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Pre-bid conferences<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Pre-bid conferences\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Bids, tenders, quotes, and proposals intersect with each other. Bids or tenders are used when the project is large and the scope of work is clear. Quotes, however, are mainly used to provide the price of particular products or services.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Bids, tenders, quotes, and proposals intersect with each other. Bids or tenders are used when the project is large and the scope of work is clear. Quotes, however, are mainly used to provide the price of particular products or services.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":42,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">8 tasks of an Agile project release have the following story points: 3, 2, 5, 5, 8, 1, 3, 5. Given that the team’s velocity is 10, how many iterations will they need to complete all of the 8 tasks?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"8 tasks of an Agile project release have the following story points: 3, 2, 5, 5, 8, 1, 3, 5. Given that the team’s velocity is 10, how many iterations will they need to complete all of the 8 tasks?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>3<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. 3\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>4<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. 4\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>5<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. 5\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>7<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. 7\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The sum of all tasks is 32 story points. Therefore, after calculation, you’ll find that it will take 3.2 iterations for the team to complete the tasks of the given release:<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">(32 story points / 10 story points = 3.2 iterations)<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\">However, since the timebox of an iteration should not be changed, 4 iterations are needed to complete the release tasks.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The sum of all tasks is 32 story points. Therefore, after calculation, you’ll find that it will take 3.2 iterations for the team to complete the tasks of the given release: (32 story points / 10 story points = 3.2 iterations) However, since the timebox of an iteration should not be changed, 4 iterations are needed to complete the release tasks.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":43,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">What defines the initial product scope? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What defines the initial product scope?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>The project budget and schedule constraints<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"The project budget and schedule constraints\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>The team's organizational structure and roles<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"The team's organizational structure and roles\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>The selected features and functions<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"The selected features and functions\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\"><p><span>The project's scope management plan<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"The project's scope management plan\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Product scope is defined as the features and functions that characterize a solution (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 102).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The scope management plan defines how to elaborate the scope (when and how), and doesn’t include the scope of work (features and functions).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Product scope is defined as the features and functions that characterize a solution (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 102). Option D: The scope management plan defines how to elaborate the scope (when and how), and doesn’t include the scope of work (features and functions).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":44,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">In business analysis, what is the primary purpose of reviewing organizational charts?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In business analysis, what is the primary purpose of reviewing organizational charts?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>To determine the budgetary constraints for implementing a new solution.<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"To determine the budgetary constraints for implementing a new solution.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>To identify the reporting structure and discover stakeholder groups or individuals who may be impacted by or have a potential impact on the solution.<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"To identify the reporting structure and discover stakeholder groups or individuals who may be impacted by or have a potential impact on the solution.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>To evaluate the performance of different departments within the organization.<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"To evaluate the performance of different departments within the organization.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\"><p><span>To assess the legal compliance of the organization’s operational procedures.<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"To assess the legal compliance of the organization’s operational procedures.\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Organizational charts help analysts understand how different roles and departments are interconnected, which can reveal key stakeholders who will be affected by or can influence the implementation of a new solution.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Organizational charts do not provide financial information or budget details. Budgetary constraints are typically assessed through financial reports, budget plans, and cost analyses, not organizational structures.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> While organizational charts show the structure and hierarchy, they do not give insights into departmental performance. Performance evaluation requires analyzing performance metrics, KPIs, and reports.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Organizational charts help analysts understand how different roles and departments are interconnected, which can reveal key stakeholders who will be affected by or can influence the implementation of a new solution. Option A: Organizational charts do not provide financial information or budget details. Budgetary constraints are typically assessed through financial reports, budget plans, and cost analyses, not organizational structures. Option C: While organizational charts show the structure and hierarchy, they do not give insights into departmental performance. Performance evaluation requires analyzing performance metrics, KPIs, and reports.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":45,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager is assigned to an amusement park project. The project comprises two phases: the first phase involves importing attractions like games and rides, and the second entails setting up and installing everything. What should the project manager do after completing the first phase?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is assigned to an amusement park project. The project comprises two phases: the first phase involves importing attractions like games and rides, and the second entails setting up and installing everything. What should the project manager do after completing the first phase?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Validate scope<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Validate scope\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Identify risks<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Identify risks\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Identify stakeholders<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Identify stakeholders\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Define activities<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Define activities\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The “Identify stakeholders” process should take place either before or concurrently while creating and approving the project charter. Stakeholders’ identification should be carried out as many times as needed. However, it should always be executed at the beginning of each project phase and whenever a significant change occurs on both the project and the organization level<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Since the first phase was complete, this means the scope has already been validated.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Risks are identified early on in the project. Nonetheless, you should keep monitoring and identifying new risks throughout the project execution.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Activities are determined during the planning stage of each project phase, unless you’re employing the rolling wave technique or adopting other life cycles rather than the traditional approach, which is not the case in this situation.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C The “Identify stakeholders” process should take place either before or concurrently while creating and approving the project charter. Stakeholders’ identification should be carried out as many times as needed. However, it should always be executed at the beginning of each project phase and whenever a significant change occurs on both the project and the organization level . Option A: Since the first phase was complete, this means the scope has already been validated. Option B: Risks are identified early on in the project. Nonetheless, you should keep monitoring and identifying new risks throughout the project execution. Option D: Activities are determined during the planning stage of each project phase, unless you’re employing the rolling wave technique or adopting other life cycles rather than the traditional approach, which is not the case in this situation.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":46,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager is working in an organization that provides products on the cloud. After a 6-month study, the organization’s R&amp;D department approved a project that will allow internet <span><\\/span>navigators to create cartoon videos using stock images, gifs, and short video clips. There will be only a $20/Month pricing plan. What type of project does this describe?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is working in an organization that provides products on the cloud. After a 6-month study, the organization’s R&D department approved a project that will allow internet navigators to create cartoon videos using stock images, gifs, and short video clips. There will be only a $20/Month pricing plan. What type of project does this describe?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Large project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Large project\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Internal project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Internal project\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Agile project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Agile project\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Traditional project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Traditional project\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">An internal project is a project in which the customer is a person or department within your company. An external project, however, is a project in which the customer is an external party, whether it is a person or an organization. The customer or the client is the person, department, or organization that is supporting the project’s development financially. The end-user of a product is not necessarily the project client or customer. Some corporations focus almost entirely on internal projects. Internet and software companies, for instance, primarily create internal projects in which they are their own client and their end-user is the general public (Fundamentals of Technology Project Management by Colleen Garton, Erika McCulloch, page 84).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Options A, C, D:<\\/span> There is no indication in the question that the project is large or that it adheres to a traditional or agile approach.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B An internal project is a project in which the customer is a person or department within your company. An external project, however, is a project in which the customer is an external party, whether it is a person or an organization. The customer or the client is the person, department, or organization that is supporting the project’s development financially. The end-user of a product is not necessarily the project client or customer. Some corporations focus almost entirely on internal projects. Internet and software companies, for instance, primarily create internal projects in which they are their own client and their end-user is the general public (Fundamentals of Technology Project Management by Colleen Garton, Erika McCulloch, page 84). Options A, C, D: There is no indication in the question that the project is large or that it adheres to a traditional or agile approach.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":47,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager presented a stadium construction project that they believe will benefit the community tremendously. Despite the mayor's agreement to carry out the project, the project manager encountered strong resistance from various stakeholders since the beginning. What should the project manager do to resolve this problem?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager presented a stadium construction project that they believe will benefit the community tremendously. Despite the mayor's agreement to carry out the project, the project manager encountered strong resistance from various stakeholders since the beginning. What should the project manager do to resolve this problem?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Create a Responsibility Assignment Matrix (RAM) to indicate which stakeholder is responsible for what aspects of the project and who needs to be consulted or informed<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Create a Responsibility Assignment Matrix (RAM) to indicate which stakeholder is responsible for what aspects of the project and who needs to be consulted or informed\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Create an organizational diagram to assign each stakeholder to the appropriate project role, allowing or disallowing certain lines of communication<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Create an organizational diagram to assign each stakeholder to the appropriate project role, allowing or disallowing certain lines of communication\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Schedule a meeting with the concerned stakeholders to thoroughly explain the project, discuss and establish ground rules, ensure their involvement, and identify any personal or organizational issues that might surface later on<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Schedule a meeting with the concerned stakeholders to thoroughly explain the project, discuss and establish ground rules, ensure their involvement, and identify any personal or organizational issues that might surface later on\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Avoid contacting these stakeholders at the start of the project and instead create a “faits accomplis” to pressure them to support the project due to a lack of alternatives<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Avoid contacting these stakeholders at the start of the project and instead create a “faits accomplis” to pressure them to support the project due to a lack of alternatives\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The project manager should schedule a meeting with the concerned stakeholders to present the project, discuss and establish ground rules, ensure their involvement, and identify any personal or organizational issues. The project manager can overcome stakeholder resistance by simply listening to their concerns. The purpose is to see things from their perspective. The project manager should understand what drives and motivates stakeholders in order to establish common ground and understand the reason behind such resistance.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C The project manager should schedule a meeting with the concerned stakeholders to present the project, discuss and establish ground rules, ensure their involvement, and identify any personal or organizational issues. The project manager can overcome stakeholder resistance by simply listening to their concerns. The purpose is to see things from their perspective. The project manager should understand what drives and motivates stakeholders in order to establish common ground and understand the reason behind such resistance.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":48,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">A project manager is assigned to lead a new project that has a predetermined budget of $170,000. Which of the following options does this situation illustrate? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is assigned to lead a new project that has a predetermined budget of $170,000. Which of the following options does this situation illustrate?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1BZ-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>    <\\/span>Assumption<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Assumption\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Expert judgment<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Expert judgment\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Constraint<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Constraint\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Functional structure<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Functional structure\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2A1-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A3-0\\\">A defined budget is a project limitation i.e. a constraint. A predetermined project budget sets the maximum amount of money that the project manager is allowed to spend on a particular project, representing a limiting factor (constraint) for the project that can impact its quality, delivery, and overall success.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C A defined budget is a project limitation i.e. a constraint. A predetermined project budget sets the maximum amount of money that the project manager is allowed to spend on a particular project, representing a limiting factor (constraint) for the project that can impact its quality, delivery, and overall success.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":49,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">A project manager consults a group of the organization’s subject matter experts on some points concerning his project. In order to ensure objectivity, the experts provided their input anonymously in order to prevent the influence of one opinion on the others. Which method is the project manager using? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager consults a group of the organization’s subject matter experts on some points concerning his project. In order to ensure objectivity, the experts provided their input anonymously in order to prevent the influence of one opinion on the others. Which method is the project manager using?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3C-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Expert Judgment <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Expert Judgment\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Delphi Technique <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Delphi Technique\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Brainstorming <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Brainstorming\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Focus groups <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Focus groups\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\"><span>Correct Answer = B<\\/span> <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\">Anonymously gathering the input of subject matter experts depicts the use of the Delphi technique, also known as the Delphi method or Delphi forecasting. This technique can be performed by sending an anonymous questionnaire or poll to gather advice from each expert, followed by a group discussion. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\" id=\\\"page_167\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Expert Judgment is too generic as an answer since it can employ several techniques such as the Delphi technique, focus groups, etc. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Brainstorming is used to generate and analyze ideas in an interactive group environment. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Focus groups bring together prequalified stakeholders and subject matter experts to openly and interactively discuss their expectations and attitudes about a proposed product, service, or result. <\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Anonymously gathering the input of subject matter experts depicts the use of the Delphi technique, also known as the Delphi method or Delphi forecasting. This technique can be performed by sending an anonymous questionnaire or poll to gather advice from each expert, followed by a group discussion. Option A: Expert Judgment is too generic as an answer since it can employ several techniques such as the Delphi technique, focus groups, etc. Option C: Brainstorming is used to generate and analyze ideas in an interactive group environment. Option D: Focus groups bring together prequalified stakeholders and subject matter experts to openly and interactively discuss their expectations and attitudes about a proposed product, service, or result.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":50,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Which category of stakeholders do subject matter experts fall into?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which category of stakeholders do subject matter experts fall into?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Business <span><\\/span>stakeholders<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Business stakeholders\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>External stakeholders<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"External stakeholders\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>Management stakeholders<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Management stakeholders\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\"><p><span>Project and product team stakeholders<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Project and product team stakeholders\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\"><span>The category of business stakeholders is a broad one, covering all those with an interest in the business; therefore, it can be made up of other role types, such as subject matter experts or users <\\/span>(PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 49).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> External stakeholders typically include the government, vendors, and customers.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Management stakeholders typically include senior managers, Project sponsors, and functional managers.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Project and product team stakeholders typically include Portfolio, program and project manager, Architects, designers, developers, Quality assurance team, etc.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The category of business stakeholders is a broad one, covering all those with an interest in the business; therefore, it can be made up of other role types, such as subject matter experts or users (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 49). Option B: External stakeholders typically include the government, vendors, and customers. Option C: Management stakeholders typically include senior managers, Project sponsors, and functional managers. Option D: Project and product team stakeholders typically include Portfolio, program and project manager, Architects, designers, developers, Quality assurance team, etc.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":51,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A business analyst is looking for analysis models to represent business workflows, system flows, and transitions. Which models would be most appropriate for this purpose? (Select two)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A business analyst is looking for analysis models to represent business workflows, system flows, and transitions. Which models would be most appropriate for this purpose? (Select two)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Process flow<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Process flow\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Data flow diagram<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Data flow diagram\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>Activity diagram<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Activity diagram\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\"><p><span>Entity relationship diagram<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Entity relationship diagram\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Context diagram<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Context diagram\"}],\"key\":[\"A\",\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A, C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">A process flow is a business analysis model that visually represents the steps the user takes while interacting with a solution. Similarly, when a system's steps are illustrated, the model is referred to as a system flow. An activity diagram, another type of process model, depicts the intricate flow of use cases. While activity diagrams share similarities with process flows in terms of syntax, they typically illustrate both user and system interactions within a single diagram, closely reflecting the textual descriptions of use cases (PMI guide to Business Analysis, pages 198 &amp; 199).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The data flow diagram is a business analysis model that integrates processes, systems, and data to illustrate the flow of information through a solution. It addresses how inputs are converted into outputs and how processes are represented.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> An Entity Relationship Diagram (ERD) is a business analysis tool that illustrates the data objects or information relevant to a business and the connections between these objects, including the cardinality of their relationships. They are more focused on data structure than on workflows or system transitions.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option E:<\\/span> A context diagram visually represents the scope of a product by illustrating a business system, such as a process, equipment, or computer system and its interactions with people and other systems (actors). The context diagram doesn’t show the detailed workflows or transitions within the system.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A, C A process flow is a business analysis model that visually represents the steps the user takes while interacting with a solution. Similarly, when a system's steps are illustrated, the model is referred to as a system flow. An activity diagram, another type of process model, depicts the intricate flow of use cases. While activity diagrams share similarities with process flows in terms of syntax, they typically illustrate both user and system interactions within a single diagram, closely reflecting the textual descriptions of use cases (PMI guide to Business Analysis, pages 198 & 199). Option B: The data flow diagram is a business analysis model that integrates processes, systems, and data to illustrate the flow of information through a solution. It addresses how inputs are converted into outputs and how processes are represented. Option D: An Entity Relationship Diagram (ERD) is a business analysis tool that illustrates the data objects or information relevant to a business and the connections between these objects, including the cardinality of their relationships. They are more focused on data structure than on workflows or system transitions. Option E: A context diagram visually represents the scope of a product by illustrating a business system, such as a process, equipment, or computer system and its interactions with people and other systems (actors). The context diagram doesn’t show the detailed workflows or transitions within the system.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":2},{\"n\":52,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager was assigned to organize a national event. The event has been planned and approved for execution. Three months separate the project manager from the big event, during which they will follow the iterative approach with 2-week long iterations. Before starting any work, the project manager holds a meeting with the sponsor, project team, stakeholders, and key contractors.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s1GS-0\\\">What kind of meeting did the project manager hold?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager was assigned to organize a national event. The event has been planned and approved for execution. Three months separate the project manager from the big event, during which they will follow the iterative approach with 2-week long iterations. Before starting any work, the project manager holds a meeting with the sponsor, project team, stakeholders, and key contractors. What kind of meeting did the project manager hold?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3BY\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Sprint planning meeting<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Sprint planning meeting\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Kick-off meeting<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Kick-off meeting\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Status meeting<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Status meeting\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Scoping meeting<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Scoping meeting\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = <span><\\/span>B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">A Project Kick-Off Meeting is considered the formal announcement of the project approval for execution. This meeting takes place at the beginning of the project, once the plan and the project itself get approved but before executing or starting any work (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 179). The Project Kick-Off Meeting is usually attended by the sponsor, other managers, the project team, as well as contractors and vendors (Effective Project Management Traditional, Agile, Extreme, Hybrid 8th edition by Robert K. Wysocki Pages 273, 274).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The sprint planning meeting can’t be the Correct Answer for the given situation because the sponsor, stakeholders, and key contractors do not usually attend this meeting.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The status meeting, on the other hand, is used to track project progress, when execution has already started.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The scoping meeting is used to define the deliverables of the project, which in this case, should have already taken place since the tournament has been planned and approved for execution as mentioned.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B A Project Kick-Off Meeting is considered the formal announcement of the project approval for execution. This meeting takes place at the beginning of the project, once the plan and the project itself get approved but before executing or starting any work (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 179). The Project Kick-Off Meeting is usually attended by the sponsor, other managers, the project team, as well as contractors and vendors (Effective Project Management Traditional, Agile, Extreme, Hybrid 8th edition by Robert K. Wysocki Pages 273, 274). Option A: The sprint planning meeting can’t be the Correct Answer for the given situation because the sponsor, stakeholders, and key contractors do not usually attend this meeting. Option C: The status meeting, on the other hand, is used to track project progress, when execution has already started. Option D: The scoping meeting is used to define the deliverables of the project, which in this case, should have already taken place since the tournament has been planned and approved for execution as mentioned.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":53,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2A3-0\\\">A project manager has been collaborating with the project sponsor to address some quality and risk-related issues. Which of the following statements concerning the role of the sponsor is true?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager has been collaborating with the project sponsor to address some quality and risk-related issues. Which of the following statements concerning the role of the sponsor is true?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1BZ-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>    <\\/span>The sponsor takes part in managing the project with the project manager.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The sponsor takes part in managing the project with the project manager.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The sponsor provides the project manager with the needed resources for completing the project.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The sponsor provides the project manager with the needed resources for completing the project.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>In a functional environment, the sponsor gives the project manager the freedom to make all decisions related to the project.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. In a functional environment, the sponsor gives the project manager the freedom to make all decisions related to the project.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The sponsor can get involved in assigning team members to particular project tasks.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The sponsor can get involved in assigning team members to particular project tasks.\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2A1-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A3-0\\\">The sponsor’s role entails providing the project manager with the required tools and resources to carry out their work.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A5-0\\\"><span>Options A &amp; D:<\\/span> The sponsor does not take part in managing the project, nor do they get involved in team members' assignments.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A5-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> In a functional environment, the project manager has very limited power, therefore they can’t have the freedom to make all decisions in this type of environment.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The sponsor’s role entails providing the project manager with the required tools and resources to carry out their work. Options A & D: The sponsor does not take part in managing the project, nor do they get involved in team members' assignments. Option C: In a functional environment, the project manager has very limited power, therefore they can’t have the freedom to make all decisions in this type of environment.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":54,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">During the sprint retrospective meeting, team members expressed frustration about wasting time going back and forth with the product owner to schedule the backlog refinement meeting. To address this issue, the project manager proposed establishing a recurring event. When should this event be scheduled?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"During the sprint retrospective meeting, team members expressed frustration about wasting time going back and forth with the product owner to schedule the backlog refinement meeting. To address this issue, the project manager proposed establishing a recurring event. When should this event be scheduled?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Right after the sprint retrospective<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Right after the sprint retrospective\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Right before the sprint planning<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Right before the sprint planning\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Right after the sprint plannin<span><\\/span>g<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Right after the sprint plannin g\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>At any time during the sprint<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. At any time during the sprint\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">In an iteration-based agile project, the product owner works with the team to refine the backlog and prepare user stories for the next iterations throughout one or multiple sessions, in the middle of the iteration (Agile Practice Guide, page 67).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D In an iteration-based agile project, the product owner works with the team to refine the backlog and prepare user stories for the next iterations throughout one or multiple sessions, in the middle of the iteration (Agile Practice Guide, page 67).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":55,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager is leading a business transformation project. As part of the project scope, a survey with 10 experts has to be conducted. During project execution, the project sponsor asked to raise the number of experts to 20, explaining that 10 experts might not provide enough input and insight. The sponsor also requested making this adjustment without issuing a change request. What should the project manager do?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is leading a business transformation project. As part of the project scope, a survey with 10 experts has to be conducted. During project execution, the project sponsor asked to raise the number of experts to 20, explaining that 10 experts might not provide enough input and insight. The sponsor also requested making this adjustment without issuing a change request. What should the project manager do?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Accommodate the change<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Accommodate the change\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Refuse to make the change<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Refuse to make the change\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Negotiate the number to reach a consensus<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Negotiate the number to reach a consensus\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Inform the sponsor that they need to follow the change management process<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Inform the sponsor that they need to follow the change management process\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Any change to the project management plan should go through the organization’s change control process by issuing a change request.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Any change to the project management plan should go through the organization’s change control process by issuing a change request.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":56,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project is behind schedule since the functional manager reassigned three team members to other projects. After negotiating with the functional manager, the project manager agreed to a temporary solution that would enable them to get one team member back for the time being, with a follow-up discussion after two weeks to re-address the issue. What conflict resolution technique did the project manager employ in this situation?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project is behind schedule since the functional manager reassigned three team members to other projects. After negotiating with the functional manager, the project manager agreed to a temporary solution that would enable them to get one team member back for the time being, with a follow-up discussion after two weeks to re-address the issue. What conflict resolution technique did the project manager employ in this situation?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Compromise<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Compromise\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Force<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Force\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Collaborate<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Collaborate\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Smooth<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Smooth\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The compromise approach to conflict resolution is characterized by searching for solutions that bring a certain level of satisfaction to all parties involved in order to temporarily or partially resolve the conflict (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 168). In the question, a temporary solution was suggested to ensure some degree of satisfaction for both the project manager and the functional manager (a lose-lose situation)<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Smoothing emphasizes areas of agreement rather than areas of difference, leading to a yield-lose situation.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The compromise approach to conflict resolution is characterized by searching for solutions that bring a certain level of satisfaction to all parties involved in order to temporarily or partially resolve the conflict (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 168). In the question, a temporary solution was suggested to ensure some degree of satisfaction for both the project manager and the functional manager (a lose-lose situation) . Option D: Smoothing emphasizes areas of agreement rather than areas of difference, leading to a yield-lose situation.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":57,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">A project manager attended a meeting to finalize a procurement that was still in the negotiation stage. However, they observed that discussions often strayed to unrelated subjects, with attendees occasionally returning to the main topic. Which of the following elements does this meeting lack? (Select two)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager attended a meeting to finalize a procurement that was still in the negotiation stage. However, they observed that discussions often strayed to unrelated subjects, with attendees occasionally returning to the main topic. Which of the following elements does this meeting lack? (Select two)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Minutes<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Minutes\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>An agenda<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. An agenda\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>An objective<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. An objective\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A facilitator<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. A facilitator\"}],\"key\":[\"B\",\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = B, D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The meeting probably does not have either a clear agenda or a facilitator. An agenda organizes and structures a meeting’s discussions, while a facilitator ensures that the agenda is being followed and respected. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Minutes of Meeting, aka MoM, is a summary of what happened during a meeting. MoM serves as a written record for future reference, thus they cannot be what caused this meeting to be chaotic.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The meeting already has an objective; concluding a procurement in the negotiation phase. But, since no one is assigned to facilitate the meeting, it’s probable that the objective was not appropriately communicated to all attendees in the first place, resulting in the described chaos.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B, D The meeting probably does not have either a clear agenda or a facilitator. An agenda organizes and structures a meeting’s discussions, while a facilitator ensures that the agenda is being followed and respected. Option A: Minutes of Meeting, aka MoM, is a summary of what happened during a meeting. MoM serves as a written record for future reference, thus they cannot be what caused this meeting to be chaotic. Option C: The meeting already has an objective; concluding a procurement in the negotiation phase. But, since no one is assigned to facilitate the meeting, it’s probable that the objective was not appropriately communicated to all attendees in the first place, resulting in the described chaos.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":2},{\"n\":58,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager is using an adaptive approach that excludes daily standups and does not employ time-boxed iterations. Which framework is the project manager implementing?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is using an adaptive approach that excludes daily standups and does not employ time-boxed iterations. Which framework is the project manager implementing?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>XP programming<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. XP programming\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Scrum<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Scrum\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>SAFE<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. SAFE\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Kanban<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Kanban\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Kanban focuses on visualizing work, managing flow, and continuous delivery using a board without specific time-boxed iterations or daily standups. All the other options use daily standups and/or increments<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Kanban focuses on visualizing work, managing flow, and continuous delivery using a board without specific time-boxed iterations or daily standups. All the other options use daily standups and/or increments\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":59,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">What are the components of the scope baseline? (Select three<span><\\/span>)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What are the components of the scope baseline? (Select three )\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\">A.<span>     <\\/span>Activities list<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Activities list\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\">B.<span>      <\\/span>Scope statement<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Scope statement\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\">C.<span>      <\\/span>WBS<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. WBS\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\">D.<span>     <\\/span>WBS dictionary<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. WBS dictionary\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\">E.<span>      <\\/span>Milestones<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. Milestones\"}],\"key\":[\"B\",\"C\",\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = B, C, D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9D-0\\\">The scope statement provides a comprehensive description of the project’s scope, including its major deliverables and exclusions. The Work Breakdown Structure (WBS) is a hierarchical decomposition of the entire scope of work required to achieve project objectives and deliver the desired outcomes. The WBS Dictionary is a comprehensive document that offers detailed information about each component in the Work Breakdown Structure (WBS). It includes specifics on deliverables, activities, and schedules, providing a clear and structured understanding of the project's elements.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B, C, D The scope statement provides a comprehensive description of the project’s scope, including its major deliverables and exclusions. The Work Breakdown Structure (WBS) is a hierarchical decomposition of the entire scope of work required to achieve project objectives and deliver the desired outcomes. The WBS Dictionary is a comprehensive document that offers detailed information about each component in the Work Breakdown Structure (WBS). It includes specifics on deliverables, activities, and schedules, providing a clear and structured understanding of the project's elements.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":60,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Shortly after starting the second phase of the project, the project manager meets with the sponsor to check if any potential players were left out in the first phase and to discuss these new stakeholders’ influence. This activity can be identified as:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Shortly after starting the second phase of the project, the project manager meets with the sponsor to check if any potential players were left out in the first phase and to discuss these new stakeholders’ influence. This activity can be identified as:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Planning stakeholder engagement<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Planning stakeholder engagement\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Identifying stakeholders<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Identifying stakeholders\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Planning resource management<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Planning resource management\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Identifying risks<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Identifying risks\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2A1-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A3-0\\\">The project manager is identifying stakeholders and analyzing their level of influence. Although the project has been active for two months, it is recommended to perform this activity on a regular basis, especially when the project gets into a new phase.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The project manager is identifying stakeholders and analyzing their level of influence. Although the project has been active for two months, it is recommended to perform this activity on a regular basis, especially when the project gets into a new phase.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":61,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">In order to review the requirements for errors and quality. What activity is performed by the team to ensure that requirements meet quality standards? (Select two)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In order to review the requirements for errors and quality. What activity is performed by the team to ensure that requirements meet quality standards? (Select two)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Inspections<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Inspections\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Requirements elicitation<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Requirements elicitation\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>Documentation<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Documentation\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\"><p><span>Peer reviews<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Peer reviews\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Audit<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Audit\"}],\"key\":[\"A\",\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A, D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">An inspection is a structured and detailed review process where an individual closely familiar with the work examines it for completeness, consistency, and conformance to both internal and external standards. This often involves using a checklist to assess requirements and offer feedback. Inspections can include walkthroughs or day-in-the-life testing. In contrast, a peer review is conducted by one or more colleagues who assess the work completed by the business analyst. This reviewer could be another business analyst, a team lead, or a quality control team member<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option E:<\\/span> An audit is performed to make sure that all processes and procedures are followed. It’s not used to review the requirements.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A, D An inspection is a structured and detailed review process where an individual closely familiar with the work examines it for completeness, consistency, and conformance to both internal and external standards. This often involves using a checklist to assess requirements and offer feedback. Inspections can include walkthroughs or day-in-the-life testing. In contrast, a peer review is conducted by one or more colleagues who assess the work completed by the business analyst. This reviewer could be another business analyst, a team lead, or a quality control team member . Option E: An audit is performed to make sure that all processes and procedures are followed. It’s not used to review the requirements.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":2},{\"n\":62,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">In order to explain to the client the meaning of a story point in the agile methodology, a project manager states that a story point can be defined as:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In order to explain to the client the meaning of a story point in the agile methodology, a project manager states that a story point can be defined as:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The equivalence of WBS in the predictive approach<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The equivalence of WBS in the predictive approach\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>An estimate of project duration<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. An estimate of project duration\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>An estimate of the required efforts to complete a particular task<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. An estimate of the required efforts to complete a particular task\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A score that is given to measure the clarity of a particular task<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. A score that is given to measure the clarity of a particular task\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9D-0\\\">A story point is a metric used to estimate the difficulty of carrying out a given user story in an agile project. In other words, it is an abstract measure of the effort required to implement a user story. A story point is simply a number that indicates the difficulty level of the story. The difficulty varies depending on the complexities, risks, and efforts involved (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 178).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C A story point is a metric used to estimate the difficulty of carrying out a given user story in an agile project. In other words, it is an abstract measure of the effort required to implement a user story. A story point is simply a number that indicates the difficulty level of the story. The difficulty varies depending on the complexities, risks, and efforts involved (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 178).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":63,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">A project manager is in charge of the construction project of a shopping center. Project work entails involving multiple subcontractors to perform paving, road connection, and parking lot lighting activities. During the project execution, the paving contractor informs the project manager that the district has increased the cost of linking the parking lot to the city drive. Which of the following communication methods should the subcontractor use to convey this information? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is in charge of the construction project of a shopping center. Project work entails involving multiple subcontractors to perform paving, road connection, and parking lot lighting activities. During the project execution, the paving contractor informs the project manager that the district has increased the cost of linking the parking lot to the city drive. Which of the following communication methods should the subcontractor use to convey this information?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1BZ-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>    <\\/span>A cost variance report<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. A cost variance report\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A formal presentation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. A formal presentation\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A memo sent to management<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. A memo sent to management\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A memo sent to the project manage<span><\\/span>r<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. A memo sent to the project manage r\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2A1-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A3-0\\\">The cost increase should be tracked and communicated using a cost variance report.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A5-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> A formal representation of the cost increase is not necessary.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A5-0\\\"><span>Options C &amp; D:<\\/span> A memo is not the appropriate means in this situation.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The cost increase should be tracked and communicated using a cost variance report. Option B: A formal representation of the cost increase is not necessary. Options C & D: A memo is not the appropriate means in this situation.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":64,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Which of the following is not a key role or responsibility of a business analyst?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following is not a key role or responsibility of a business analyst?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Requirements elicitation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Requirements elicitation\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Traceability and monitoring<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Traceability and monitoring\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholder engagement<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Stakeholder engagement\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Quality assurance<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Quality assurance\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">While business analysts may define acceptance criteria and ensure that the requirements are met, the actual process of quality assurance, including testing and validation, is typically the responsibility of a dedicated QA team<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Requirements elicitation is the activity of extracting information from stakeholders and various sources to gain a deeper understanding of the business needs. This aims to address a problem or seize an opportunity, while also considering the stakeholders' preferences and conditions for the solution that will meet those needs.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Traceability and monitoring Involves the processes for tracking, approving, and evaluating changes to product information, ensuring effective management throughout the business analysis effort.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Stakeholder Engagement encompasses the processes involved in identifying and analyzing individuals and groups interested in the solution. It determines the most effective methods for engaging, communicating, and collaborating with these stakeholders. The goal is to establish a shared understanding of the necessary business analysis activities to define the solution. It also includes conducting periodic assessments of the business analysis process to ensure its effectiveness.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D While business analysts may define acceptance criteria and ensure that the requirements are met, the actual process of quality assurance, including testing and validation, is typically the responsibility of a dedicated QA team Option A: Requirements elicitation is the activity of extracting information from stakeholders and various sources to gain a deeper understanding of the business needs. This aims to address a problem or seize an opportunity, while also considering the stakeholders' preferences and conditions for the solution that will meet those needs. Option B: Traceability and monitoring Involves the processes for tracking, approving, and evaluating changes to product information, ensuring effective management throughout the business analysis effort. Option C: Stakeholder Engagement encompasses the processes involved in identifying and analyzing individuals and groups interested in the solution. It determines the most effective methods for engaging, communicating, and collaborating with these stakeholders. The goal is to establish a shared understanding of the necessary business analysis activities to define the solution. It also includes conducting periodic assessments of the business analysis process to ensure its effectiveness.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":65,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager of a distressed project had been replaced by a new one. While the new project manager was examining the network diagram, they found five critical paths and two near-critical paths. What does this indicate about the project?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager of a distressed project had been replaced by a new one. While the new project manager was examining the network diagram, they found five critical paths and two near-critical paths. What does this indicate about the project?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project is at a high risk<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The project is at a high risk\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project requires more financial or human resources<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The project requires more financial or human resources\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project will be completed on time and within budget<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The project will be completed on time and within budget\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project should be terminated<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The project should be terminated\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">According to the network diagram, the project is at high risk. With five critical paths and two near-critical paths, any delay of any activity belonging to these paths will result in the whole project’s delay. Having more than one critical and near-critical path does not mean that the project requires more resources and an increase in the allocated budget. On the other hand, just because the project is at high risk of schedule delay does not mean it should be terminated<span><\\/span>.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A According to the network diagram, the project is at high risk. With five critical paths and two near-critical paths, any delay of any activity belonging to these paths will result in the whole project’s delay. Having more than one critical and near-critical path does not mean that the project requires more resources and an increase in the allocated budget. On the other hand, just because the project is at high risk of schedule delay does not mean it should be terminated .\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":66,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">To ensure that the scope and performance are validated, who should the business analyst address to gain formal acceptance of the deliverables?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"To ensure that the scope and performance are validated, who should the business analyst address to gain formal acceptance of the deliverables?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Project manager<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Project manager\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Project sponsor<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Project sponsor\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>Project team<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Project team\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\"><p><span>End users<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"End users\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Scope and performance validation includes scheduled meetings with the sponsor or customer to formally obtain acceptance of the deliverables. The task of evaluating solution performance is typically led by the business analyst or someone fulfilling that role.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> End users provide feedback and may perform testing, but the formal acceptance usually comes from the project sponsor, who represents the business's interests.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Scope and performance validation includes scheduled meetings with the sponsor or customer to formally obtain acceptance of the deliverables. The task of evaluating solution performance is typically led by the business analyst or someone fulfilling that role. Option D: End users provide feedback and may perform testing, but the formal acceptance usually comes from the project sponsor, who represents the business's interests.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":67,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager is managing a project for a startup that needs to quickly deliver a Minimum Viable Product (MVP) to capture an opportunity in the market. Which of the following development approaches would be best suited for focusing on delivering value as quickly as possible?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is managing a project for a startup that needs to quickly deliver a Minimum Viable Product (MVP) to capture an opportunity in the market. Which of the following development approaches would be best suited for focusing on delivering value as quickly as possible?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Hybrid<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Hybrid\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Predictive<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Predictive\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Incremental<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Incremental\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Iterative<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Iterative\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">In the incremental development approach, the deliverable is incrementally enhanced by adding functionality in successive iterations until it meets the required capabilities and is deemed complete. It provides finished deliverables such as the MVP that the customer may be able to use immediately.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The hybrid approach, as defined in the agile guide, is “a combination of two or more agile and non-agile elements, having a non-agile end result.”<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The predictive approach, often referred to as Waterfall, involves detailed planning and a linear approach. It is not well-suited for situations where the focus is on value delivery at the beginning of the project.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The iterative development approach begins with a basic implementation and gradually enhances it by adding features over time until the final product is fully developed. It allows feedback on partially completed work to improve the work.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C In the incremental development approach, the deliverable is incrementally enhanced by adding functionality in successive iterations until it meets the required capabilities and is deemed complete. It provides finished deliverables such as the MVP that the customer may be able to use immediately. Option A: The hybrid approach, as defined in the agile guide, is “a combination of two or more agile and non-agile elements, having a non-agile end result.” Option B: The predictive approach, often referred to as Waterfall, involves detailed planning and a linear approach. It is not well-suited for situations where the focus is on value delivery at the beginning of the project. Option D: The iterative development approach begins with a basic implementation and gradually enhances it by adding features over time until the final product is fully developed. It allows feedback on partially completed work to improve the work.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":68,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">In the plan schedule management process, which tool is used to prepare the schedule management plan?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In the plan schedule management process, which tool is used to prepare the schedule management plan?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Data analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Data analysis\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Data collection<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Data collection\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Decomposition<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Decomposition\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Rolling wave planning<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Rolling wave planning\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Data analysis includes techniques such as the alternatives analysis which is used to evaluate identified options in order to select the options or approaches to use to execute and perform project work. Data analysis techniques are used to organize, assess, and evaluate data and information (PMI Process Groups Guide, page 89).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Data collection refers to gathering information, meaning it’s not a tool used to “plan schedule management”.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Options C &amp; D:<\\/span> Decomposition and rolling wave planning are techniques used for the “define activities” process rather than “plan schedule management” process.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Data analysis includes techniques such as the alternatives analysis which is used to evaluate identified options in order to select the options or approaches to use to execute and perform project work. Data analysis techniques are used to organize, assess, and evaluate data and information (PMI Process Groups Guide, page 89). Option B: Data collection refers to gathering information, meaning it’s not a tool used to “plan schedule management”. Options C & D: Decomposition and rolling wave planning are techniques used for the “define activities” process rather than “plan schedule management” process.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":69,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2A3-0\\\">A project manager is leading a project for developing an online furniture store. Developing the online store internally would cost $100,000, plus a $3,000 monthly maintenance fee. When exploring the option of developing the online store externally, the project manager received an offer from a vendor to create the store for $50,000 plus $4 per transaction to administer the e-store, knowing that the online store would potentially have an average of 1000 transactions per month during the first year. Which of the following methods can help the project manager determine and choose the best option?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is leading a project for developing an online furniture store. Developing the online store internally would cost $100,000, plus a $3,000 monthly maintenance fee. When exploring the option of developing the online store externally, the project manager received an offer from a vendor to create the store for $50,000 plus $4 per transaction to administer the e-store, knowing that the online store would potentially have an average of 1000 transactions per month during the first year. Which of the following methods can help the project manager determine and choose the best option?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1BZ-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>    <\\/span>Pareto chart<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Pareto chart\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Control chart<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Control chart\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Decision tree<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Decision tree\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Trend analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Trend analysis\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2A1-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A3-0\\\">The decision tree method can help the project manager choose the best option for their project. Decision trees are used to support the selection of the best course of action among several alternative possible options. The decision tree uses branches representing the different decisions or events and their associated costs and risks.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A5-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> A Pareto chart is mostly used to display and prioritize the various root causes of a problem or an error<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A5-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Control charts display trends and sampling results and are used to determine whether a process is stable or has predictable performance.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A5-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Trend analysis can predict future trends and outcomes based on historical data.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C The decision tree method can help the project manager choose the best option for their project. Decision trees are used to support the selection of the best course of action among several alternative possible options. The decision tree uses branches representing the different decisions or events and their associated costs and risks. Option A: A Pareto chart is mostly used to display and prioritize the various root causes of a problem or an error . Option B: Control charts display trends and sampling results and are used to determine whether a process is stable or has predictable performance. Option D: Trend analysis can predict future trends and outcomes based on historical data.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":70,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">A project manager is carrying out the initial planning activities for a gas pipeline construction project. While estimating the installation activity, one team member mentioned that they completed the same length of pipes in 14 hours during a previous similar project. Another team member asserts that they can install 100 meters of gas pipes per hour. The team will need to run a total of 1000 meters of pipes. Using the analogous estimating technique, how many hours will it take the team to run the gas pipeline?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is carrying out the initial planning activities for a gas pipeline construction project. While estimating the installation activity, one team member mentioned that they completed the same length of pipes in 14 hours during a previous similar project. Another team member asserts that they can install 100 meters of gas pipes per hour. The team will need to run a total of 1000 meters of pipes. Using the analogous estimating technique, how many hours will it take the team to run the gas pipeline?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>10<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. 10\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>11<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. 11\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>12<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. 12\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>14<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. 14\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Unlike parametric estimating, the analogous estimating technique uses expert judgment by comparing a particular activity to a similarly completed one on a previous project in order to determine its duration or cost. This means that the project manager should rely on expert feedback, i.e., completing a similar task in 14 hours.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Unlike parametric estimating, the analogous estimating technique uses expert judgment by comparing a particular activity to a similarly completed one on a previous project in order to determine its duration or cost. This means that the project manager should rely on expert feedback, i.e., completing a similar task in 14 hours.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":71,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Which of the following statements best describes the application of systems thinking at the organizational level?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following statements best describes the application of systems thinking at the organizational level?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p>Systems thinking focuses solely on analyzing detailed components of an organization without considering their interactions. <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Systems thinking focuses solely on analyzing detailed components of an organization without considering their interactions.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-1\\\"><p><span>Applying systems thinking involves recognizing an organization as a system composed of people, processes, and tools, and understanding how changes to one component can affect other related components.<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Applying systems thinking involves recognizing an organization as a system composed of people, processes, and tools, and understanding how changes to one component can affect other related components.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-1\\\"><p><span>Systems thinking is primarily concerned with the external factors impacting an organization and does not require analysis of internal component relationships.<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Systems thinking is primarily concerned with the external factors impacting an organization and does not require analysis of internal component relationships.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-1\\\"><p><span>Systems thinking is limited to understanding the interactions between people and processes, excluding tools from the analysis.<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Systems thinking is limited to understanding the interactions between people and processes, excluding tools from the analysis.\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Systems thinking requires both a holistic and detailed perspective, focusing on the organization as a system of interconnected parts. Systems thinking involves recognizing the organization as a collection of people, processes, and tools and analyzing how changes in one component can impact other related components. This comprehensive view is essential to effectively manage organizational changes and understand their broader implications (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 370).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Systems thinking requires both a holistic and detailed perspective, focusing on the organization as a system of interconnected parts. Systems thinking involves recognizing the organization as a collection of people, processes, and tools and analyzing how changes in one component can impact other related components. This comprehensive view is essential to effectively manage organizational changes and understand their broader implications (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 370).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":72,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager is responsible for leading a hybrid project with remote team members dispersed across four continents. As a result, the team has experienced communication issues. What can the project manager do to alleviate the team’s communication challenges? (Select two)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is responsible for leading a hybrid project with remote team members dispersed across four continents. As a result, the team has experienced communication issues. What can the project manager do to alleviate the team’s communication challenges? (Select two)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Set up remote pairing<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Set up remote pairing\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Use an agile approach for the project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Use an agile approach for the project\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Colocate the team<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Colocate the team\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Create fishbowl windows<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Create fishbowl windows\"}],\"key\":[\"A\",\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A, D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Fishbowl windows and remote pairing are two techniques used to manage communication in remote teams. The project manager can create fishbowl windows by initiating long-lived video conferences, where team members join in at the beginning of the workday and leave at the end. Remote pairing, on the other hand, is when two or more people join an online event at a specific time to discuss and share screens when needed (Agile Practice Guide, page 46).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Changing the project life cycle from hybrid to agile won't have any significant impact on communication if team members don't take any specific measures or techniques to improve the way they interact with each other.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Colocating the team is not always feasible due to many considerations such as cost, talent availability, regulations, etc. However, when possible, getting the team together in person on a regular basis is a good practice.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A, D Fishbowl windows and remote pairing are two techniques used to manage communication in remote teams. The project manager can create fishbowl windows by initiating long-lived video conferences, where team members join in at the beginning of the workday and leave at the end. Remote pairing, on the other hand, is when two or more people join an online event at a specific time to discuss and share screens when needed (Agile Practice Guide, page 46). Option B: Changing the project life cycle from hybrid to agile won't have any significant impact on communication if team members don't take any specific measures or techniques to improve the way they interact with each other. Option C: Colocating the team is not always feasible due to many considerations such as cost, talent availability, regulations, etc. However, when possible, getting the team together in person on a regular basis is a good practice.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":2},{\"n\":73,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">A stakeholder is pressuring the project team to make some changes to the final product. The project manager informs the client that the changes cannot be implemented immediately due to the organization’s established processes. Which of the following documents these processes? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A stakeholder is pressuring the project team to make some changes to the final product. The project manager informs the client that the changes cannot be implemented immediately due to the organization’s established processes. Which of the following documents these processes?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1BZ-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>    <\\/span>The change control board<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The change control board\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The change control system<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The change control system\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The organizational process assets<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The organizational process assets\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The scope management plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The scope management plan\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\"><span>Correct Answer = B<\\/span> <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\">The Change Control System is a set of procedures that describes how modifications to the project deliverables and documentation are managed and controlled (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 237). <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The Change Control Board (CCB) is responsible for reviewing, evaluating, approving, delaying, or rejecting changes to the project. Not every project has a change control board. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The organizational process assets refer to plans, processes, guidelines, and knowledge repositories that are unique to and employed by the organization. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\" id=\\\"page_173\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The scope management plan, on the other hand, only explains the scope's definition, development, monitoring, control, and validation procedures. <\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The Change Control System is a set of procedures that describes how modifications to the project deliverables and documentation are managed and controlled (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 237). Option A: The Change Control Board (CCB) is responsible for reviewing, evaluating, approving, delaying, or rejecting changes to the project. Not every project has a change control board. Option C: The organizational process assets refer to plans, processes, guidelines, and knowledge repositories that are unique to and employed by the organization. Option D: The scope management plan, on the other hand, only explains the scope's definition, development, monitoring, control, and validation procedures.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":74,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Wanting to have their own home, a couple decided to build a tiny house and started planning for the project. However, when it came to interior design, they seemed to disagree on many details. Since the couple wanted to get their house ready by the end of the year, they decided to launch the construction work first and decide about the interior design details later on. What technique did the couple use?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Wanting to have their own home, a couple decided to build a tiny house and started planning for the project. However, when it came to interior design, they seemed to disagree on many details. Since the couple wanted to get their house ready by the end of the year, they decided to launch the construction work first and decide about the interior design details later on. What technique did the couple use?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Rolling wave<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Rolling wave\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Fast-tracking<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Fast-tracking\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Crashing<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Crashing\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Decomposition<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Decomposition\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The Rolling wave method is used to address uncertainty by planning near-term work in detail while planning future tasks in a broader (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 249). It’s a form of progressive elaboration that sets up near-term plans and “rolls” into the longer term as more details become available. In this way, rolling wave planning allows work to progress in current and near-term deliverables while planning for potential work packages continues.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The Rolling wave method is used to address uncertainty by planning near-term work in detail while planning future tasks in a broader (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 249). It’s a form of progressive elaboration that sets up near-term plans and “rolls” into the longer term as more details become available. In this way, rolling wave planning allows work to progress in current and near-term deliverables while planning for potential work packages continues.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":75,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager asked the project team to perform benchmarking, brainstorming sessions, focus groups, interviews, and questionnaires. What are these tools and techniques used for?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager asked the project team to perform benchmarking, brainstorming sessions, focus groups, interviews, and questionnaires. What are these tools and techniques used for?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Data analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Data analysis\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Data gathering<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Data gathering\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Data representation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Data representation\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Decision making<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Decision making\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">In this case, the project is currently in the Collect Requirements process, which involves identifying and documenting the needs and requirements of stakeholders. Data gathering takes part in the Collect Requirements process to obtain stakeholders’ requirements. It puts in use tools and techniques like benchmarking, brainstorming, focus groups, interviews, questionnaires, and surveys.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B In this case, the project is currently in the Collect Requirements process, which involves identifying and documenting the needs and requirements of stakeholders. Data gathering takes part in the Collect Requirements process to obtain stakeholders’ requirements. It puts in use tools and techniques like benchmarking, brainstorming, focus groups, interviews, questionnaires, and surveys.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":76,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">To collect more funding, a project manager sends their project’s business case to an investor who happens to be quite demanding, as they might reject a project because its goal is not SMART. What does “S” stand for?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"To collect more funding, a project manager sends their project’s business case to an investor who happens to be quite demanding, as they might reject a project because its goal is not SMART. What does “S” stand for?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Specific<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Specific\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Simple<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Simple\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Smart<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Smart\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Safe<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Safe\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">SMART is an acronym that stands for Specific, Meaningful, Achievable, Relevant, and Timely (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 97). Each letter in SMART can have other alternatives, except the “S” which commonly refers to “Specific” or “Strategic and Specific”.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A SMART is an acronym that stands for Specific, Meaningful, Achievable, Relevant, and Timely (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 97). Each letter in SMART can have other alternatives, except the “S” which commonly refers to “Specific” or “Strategic and Specific”.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":77,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">In which process group do stakeholders have the most influence over a project?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In which process group do stakeholders have the most influence over a project?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Initiating<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Initiating\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Planning<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Planning\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Executin<span><\\/span>g<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Executin g\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Closing<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Closing\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Stakeholders have the most influence and impact on a predictive project at its early stages. Stakeholder influence is mostly perceived in the early stages of the project. The project is flexible at this stage and can be changed and stakeholders generally take advantage of this. Once it starts to progress, the project takes on momentum and power of its own, thus, the cost of stopping it or altering its direction becomes very high.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Stakeholders have the most influence and impact on a predictive project at its early stages. Stakeholder influence is mostly perceived in the early stages of the project. The project is flexible at this stage and can be changed and stakeholders generally take advantage of this. Once it starts to progress, the project takes on momentum and power of its own, thus, the cost of stopping it or altering its direction becomes very high.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":78,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">Which of the following Fixed-price contracts should be used for currency fluctuations? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following Fixed-price contracts should be used for currency fluctuations?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3C-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Fixed Price with Currency Adjustments <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Fixed Price with Currency Adjustments\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Fixed Price with Economic Price Adjustments <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Fixed Price with Economic Price Adjustments\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Fixed Price Incentive Fee <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Fixed Price Incentive Fee\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Firm Fixed Fee <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Firm Fixed Fee\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\"><span>Correct Answer = B<\\/span> <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\">Currency fluctuations can be handled using a Fixed Price with Economic Price Adjustment (FP-EPA) contract. This type of contract allows the adjustment of the fixed price or rate of the contract. The buyer and seller agree on pre-defined criteria for this adjustment. This is often used for long-term projects that can span multiple years to adapt to market uncertainties and changes. The criteria to adjust the fixed price are based on market conditions that are beyond the control of both the buyer and seller, including changes in the cost of labor and material, general inflation, and fluctuations in the currency market. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> In a Fixed Price Incentive Fee Contract (FPIF), the buyer pays the seller a defined amount plus an additional incentive if the seller meets defined performance criteria. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> A Firm Fixed Price Contract (FFP) includes a fixed price that the buyer pays the seller regardless of the seller’s costs. Fixed Price with Currency Adjustment is a made-up term.<span><\\/span> <\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Currency fluctuations can be handled using a Fixed Price with Economic Price Adjustment (FP-EPA) contract. This type of contract allows the adjustment of the fixed price or rate of the contract. The buyer and seller agree on pre-defined criteria for this adjustment. This is often used for long-term projects that can span multiple years to adapt to market uncertainties and changes. The criteria to adjust the fixed price are based on market conditions that are beyond the control of both the buyer and seller, including changes in the cost of labor and material, general inflation, and fluctuations in the currency market. Option C: In a Fixed Price Incentive Fee Contract (FPIF), the buyer pays the seller a defined amount plus an additional incentive if the seller meets defined performance criteria. Option D: A Firm Fixed Price Contract (FFP) includes a fixed price that the buyer pays the seller regardless of the seller’s costs. Fixed Price with Currency Adjustment is a made-up term.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":79,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">A web development project is planned with a series of tasks scheduled over a three-month period.  The initial schedule has a high workload for the developers in certain weeks, leading to potential burnout and inefficiencies. The project manager used the resource smoothing technique to balance the workload. What should the project manager do next?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A web development project is planned with a series of tasks scheduled over a three-month period.  The initial schedule has a high workload for the developers in certain weeks, leading to potential burnout and inefficiencies. The project manager used the resource smoothing technique to balance the workload. What should the project manager do next?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Update the project calendar<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Update the project calendar\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Update the schedule management plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Update the schedule management plan\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Update stakeholder engagement plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Update stakeholder engagement plan\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Update the requirements management plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Update the requirements management plan\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The project calendar outlines the available working days and shifts for scheduling project activities.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> While the schedule management plan outlines how the schedule will be developed, monitored and controlled, the immediate task after the resource smoothing technique is to update the project calendar.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The stakeholder engagement plan, which is a key part of the project management plan, outlines strategies and actions to ensure productive stakeholder involvement in decision-making and execution. It can be formal or informal, detailed or broad, depending on the project's needs and stakeholder expectations. It’s not affected by resource smoothing techniques.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The project requirements management plan describes how requirements will be analyzed, documented, and managed. It’s not affected by the resource smoothing technique unless the activity will affect the project’s scope and/or requirements.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The project calendar outlines the available working days and shifts for scheduling project activities. Option B: While the schedule management plan outlines how the schedule will be developed, monitored and controlled, the immediate task after the resource smoothing technique is to update the project calendar. Option C: The stakeholder engagement plan, which is a key part of the project management plan, outlines strategies and actions to ensure productive stakeholder involvement in decision-making and execution. It can be formal or informal, detailed or broad, depending on the project's needs and stakeholder expectations. It’s not affected by resource smoothing techniques. Option D: The project requirements management plan describes how requirements will be analyzed, documented, and managed. It’s not affected by the resource smoothing technique unless the activity will affect the project’s scope and/or requirements.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":80,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager is in charge of an ergonomic chair design project. Upon the identification of some technical risks, the project manager decides it’s best to create a prototype. This is an example of risk:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is in charge of an ergonomic chair design project. Upon the identification of some technical risks, the project manager decides it’s best to create a prototype. This is an example of risk:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Acceptance<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Acceptance\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Avoidance<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Avoidance\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Transfer<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Transfer\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Mitigation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Mitigation\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Risk mitigation can imply prototype development in order to prevent the risk from scaling up. Creating a prototype will support the testing and through testing, you can generate the necessary data to probably even close the risk. To keep costs low, you can opt for partial prototypes for the specific portions of the process that involve the risk.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Risk mitigation can imply prototype development in order to prevent the risk from scaling up. Creating a prototype will support the testing and through testing, you can generate the necessary data to probably even close the risk. To keep costs low, you can opt for partial prototypes for the specific portions of the process that involve the risk.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":81,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A business analyst is tasked with leading the development of a new product for their company. The goal is to ensure the new product meets market needs and aligns with the company's strategic objectives. What should the business analyst perform?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A business analyst is tasked with leading the development of a new product for their company. The goal is to ensure the new product meets market needs and aligns with the company's strategic objectives. What should the business analyst perform?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Conduct market research<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Conduct market research\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Develop a detailed project plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Develop a detailed project plan\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Benchmarking<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Benchmarking\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Gap analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Gap analysis\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>E.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>Create a marketing strategy for the new product<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. Create a marketing strategy for the new product\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9D-0\\\">Gap analysis involves comparing the current state with the desired future state to identify any gaps that need to be addressed. It ensures that the product development aligns with the strategic objectives and market needs.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> While market analysis is the activity of collecting information about factors that influence a marketplace, it does not take into account the company’s strategic objectives.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Developing a project plan comes after the initial research and analysis to ensure the plan is based on accurate market insights and identified gaps.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Benchmarking involves comparing an organization’s products, services, and processes to industry best performance and practices from other competitors.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Gap analysis involves comparing the current state with the desired future state to identify any gaps that need to be addressed. It ensures that the product development aligns with the strategic objectives and market needs. Option A: While market analysis is the activity of collecting information about factors that influence a marketplace, it does not take into account the company’s strategic objectives. Option B: Developing a project plan comes after the initial research and analysis to ensure the plan is based on accurate market insights and identified gaps. Option C: Benchmarking involves comparing an organization’s products, services, and processes to industry best performance and practices from other competitors.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":82,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">A program manager oversees multiple project teams, each working on different projects and conducts its own daily standup meeting separately. Each team has an assigned member to attend a regular status meeting, Which methodology is being implemented?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A program manager oversees multiple project teams, each working on different projects and conducts its own daily standup meeting separately. Each team has an assigned member to attend a regular status meeting, Which methodology is being implemented?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Scrum of scrums <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Scrum of scrums\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>SAFE<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. SAFE\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>LeS<span><\\/span>S<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. LeS S\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>FDD<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. FDD\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The daily scrum or daily stand-up meeting is a daily huddle meeting where the development team members inspect progress toward the Sprint goal, adjust the upcoming planned work, and raise encountered obstacles or impediments.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The Scrum of Scrums technique is used when two or more Scrum teams consisting of three to nine members each need to coordinate their work instead of one large Scrum team. A representative from each team attends a meeting with the other team representative(s) (Agile Practice Guide, page 126)<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Large Scale Scrum (LeSS) is a framework designed to coordinate multiple development teams working towards a unified goal (Agile practice guide, page 128). Its central principle is to preserve as many elements of the standard single-team Scrum model as possible, thereby minimizing extensions that could introduce unnecessary complexity.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The daily scrum or daily stand-up meeting is a daily huddle meeting where the development team members inspect progress toward the Sprint goal, adjust the upcoming planned work, and raise encountered obstacles or impediments. The Scrum of Scrums technique is used when two or more Scrum teams consisting of three to nine members each need to coordinate their work instead of one large Scrum team. A representative from each team attends a meeting with the other team representative(s) (Agile Practice Guide, page 126) . Option C: Large Scale Scrum (LeSS) is a framework designed to coordinate multiple development teams working towards a unified goal (Agile practice guide, page 128). Its central principle is to preserve as many elements of the standard single-team Scrum model as possible, thereby minimizing extensions that could introduce unnecessary complexity.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":83,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">A project manager got the approval to carry out a significant change that would bring added value to the project. The change has a total cost of $10,000 and will add one month to the project’s duration. What should the project manager do right after getting the change approved? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager got the approval to carry out a significant change that would bring added value to the project. The change has a total cost of $10,000 and will add one month to the project’s duration. What should the project manager do right after getting the change approved?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1BZ-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>    <\\/span>Call for a meeting with the CCB to review the change<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Call for a meeting with the CCB to review the change\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Update the time, cost, and scope baselines to reflect the change<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Update the time, cost, and scope baselines to reflect the change\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Perform a change risk assessment<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Perform a change risk assessment\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Update the change control system to reflect the change<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Update the change control system to reflect the change\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2A1-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A3-0\\\">As soon as a change gets approved, the project manager must update the time, cost, and scope baselines to reflect the impact of the change on all project aspects.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A5-0\\\"><span>Options A &amp; C:<\\/span> Each change gets through review as well as risk assessment by the Change Control Board (CCB) before getting approved or rejected.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A5-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> A change control system represents a description of the way changes to the project scope should be managed. Actual changes are not part of the change control system.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B As soon as a change gets approved, the project manager must update the time, cost, and scope baselines to reflect the impact of the change on all project aspects. Options A & C: Each change gets through review as well as risk assessment by the Change Control Board (CCB) before getting approved or rejected. Option D: A change control system represents a description of the way changes to the project scope should be managed. Actual changes are not part of the change control system.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":84,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">The project team did not understand the project requirements. Who’s responsible for requirements elicitation?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The project team did not understand the project requirements. Who’s responsible for requirements elicitation?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project manager<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Project manager\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Business analyst<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Business analyst\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project manager and business analyst<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Project manager and business analyst\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project sponsor<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Project sponsor\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The business analyst is the one responsible for gathering, analyzing, and documenting the requirements. They ensure that the project team understands what needs to be built.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The project manager manages the overall project, ensuring that it is delivered on time, within scope, and within budget. They may be involved in requirements gathering but do not usually have the primary responsibility.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> In some projects, especially larger or more complex ones, the project manager and business analyst may collaborate closely to ensure requirements are well-understood and documented.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The project sponsor is responsible for authorizing the project.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The business analyst is the one responsible for gathering, analyzing, and documenting the requirements. They ensure that the project team understands what needs to be built. Option A: The project manager manages the overall project, ensuring that it is delivered on time, within scope, and within budget. They may be involved in requirements gathering but do not usually have the primary responsibility. Option C: In some projects, especially larger or more complex ones, the project manager and business analyst may collaborate closely to ensure requirements are well-understood and documented. Option D: The project sponsor is responsible for authorizing the project.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":85,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sFM-0\\\">Match the statements concerning the tasks of a hybrid project with their right classification:<\\/p><div class=\\\"class_sFS-0\\\"><img alt=\\\"Source figure\\\" loading=\\\"lazy\\\" src=\\\"data:image/jpeg;base64,";
